    10	which way each theme it weighed pushes it; theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round, and a theme judgement that says
    11	changed queues every open asset thesis with evidence in force, once. The round's queue is derived from the ledger (the day's changed
    12	views, the dependants of views judged at this sequence number with a changed conclusion, and the asset theses a changed theme queues),
    13	so a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit had queued.
    14	
    15	The evidence in view (D198): a judgement reads the arrivals and the basis among the evidence in force, not everything in force.
    16	
    17	The reference (D260): the rung is the forecast the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects
