model; under the partnership the AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services while NVIDIA earns both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. No commitment amounts, counterparties or credit-support sizes are disclosed.", "passages": ["NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.", "This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity."], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.", "This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity."], "original_party": "NVIDIA Corporation", "reporting_speaker": "NVIDIA Corporation", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "8:e1", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "NVIDIA published a statement on its official website on July 1 announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure and to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers and corporate clients. NVIDIA said it will earn not only standard product revenue but also an additional share of cloud service revenue, creating a usage-based recurring revenue stream; a NVIDIA spokesperson confirmed the program, internally called the 'AI Compute Partnership.'", "passages": ["On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.", "According to NVIDIA’s official press release, the company will earn not only standard product revenue but also an additional share of cloud service revenue, creating a usage-based, recurring revenue stream.", "A NVIDIA spokesperson also confirmed the existence of the program."], "verified_passages": ["On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.", "According to NVIDIA’s official press release, the company will earn not only standard product revenue but also an additional share of cloud service revenue, creating a usage-based, recurring revenue stream.", "A NVIDIA spokesperson also confirmed the existence of the program."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing NVIDIA official statement/press release)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "16:e1", "article": 16, "input_id": "gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5", "title": "Nvidia launches revenue-sharing model for AI startups", "publisher": "qz.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "NVIDIA announced a revenue-sharing program (announced on a Wednesday, reported 2026-07-02) under which AI startups, model builders and enterprises get access to Nvidia-powered computing infrastructure without having to finance hardware buildouts themselves; revenue from both product sales and cloud operations flows back to Nvidia as AI cloud companies sell Nvidia-powered services to end customers. Nvidia's Kress, in a blog post, described the resulting income as a \"recurring, usage-linked earnings stream\" for Nvidia and said the model removes the need for customers to handle site selection, power procurement, construction and hardware bring-up. Token credits are also part of the offering, letting startups access compute without upfront capital outlays. No revenue figure or contract value was disclosed.", "passages": ["The chipmaker will earn a share of cloud revenue from partners, with two data center operators named as its first participants", "Nvidia $NVDA announced a revenue-sharing program on Wednesday designed to give AI startups, model builders, and enterprises access to its computing infrastructure without requiring them to finance hardware buildouts themselves.", "Revenue from both product sales and cloud operations flows back to Nvidia under the arrangement, as AI cloud companies provide Nvidia -powered services to their end customers. Kress, writing in a blog post, called the resulting income a \"recurring, usage-linked earnings stream\" for Nvidia ; on the customer side, she said the model removes the need to navigate site selection, power procurement, construction, and hardware bring-up before accessing large-scale compute.", "Token credits are also part of the offering, giving startups a way to access compute resources without upfront capital outlays."], "verified_passages": ["The chipmaker will earn a share of cloud revenue from partners, with two data center operators named as its first participants", "Nvidia $NVDA announced a revenue-sharing program on Wednesday designed to give AI startups, model builders, and enterprises access to its computing infrastructure without requiring them to finance hardware buildouts themselves.", "Revenue from both product sales and cloud operations flows back to Nvidia under the arrangement, as AI cloud companies provide Nvidia -powered services to their end customers. Kress, writing in a blog post, called the resulting income a \"recurring, usage-linked earnings stream\" for Nvidia ; on the customer side, she said the model removes the need to navigate site selection, power procurement, construction, and hardware bring-up before accessing large-scale compute.", "Token credits are also part of the offering, giving startups a way to access compute resources without upfront capital outlays."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "qz.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "Wednesday", "evidence_period": "from July 2026 onward", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "18:e1", "article": 18, "input_id": "gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0", "title": "Nvidia acts as backstop for customer GPUs in return for cut of cloud revenue", "publisher": "datacenterdynamics.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia is acting as a financial backstop for neocloud customers buying its AI chips, agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate in exchange for a share of the customers' cloud revenue, per a company post detailing the new offering. Nvidia said the model lets AI clouds procure Nvidia infrastructure through 'economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model,' with Nvidia earning both standard product revenue and a share of cloud revenue on the supported capacity, and it described this as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream that accelerates adoption of Nvidia platforms among AI-native customers. Firmus and Sharon AI are named among the first companies to have adopted the offer.", "passages": ["Nvidia is supporting neocloud customers in purchasing its AI chips.\nThe chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\nThe backstop sees Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate. Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to have adopted the offer.", "\"This new model enables AI clouds to procure Nvidia infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.", "\"Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell Nvidia-powered cloud services, with Nvidia earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides Nvidia with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\""], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia is supporting neocloud customers in purchasing its AI chips.\nThe chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\nThe backstop sees Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate. Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to have adopted the offer.", "\"This new model enables AI clouds to procure Nvidia infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.", "\"Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell Nvidia-powered cloud services, with Nvidia earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides Nvidia with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\""], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Georgia Butler, datacenterdynamics.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v6", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "21:e1", "article": 21, "input_id": "gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816", "title": "Nvidia offers to take a cut of AI cloud revenue on top of hardware sales in new optional financing vehicle — trades tokens for revenue cut", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "NVIDIA announced a new \"revenue-sharing and credit-support model\" in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress: partner AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, and NVIDIA collects its usual hardware product revenue plus a percentage of the cloud income earned on that capacity, described as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream. Per Bloomberg, developers receive token credits in exchange for a slice of their future sales; neither NVIDIA nor its partners has disclosed the revenue-split percentages. Australia's Sharon AI and Singapore-based Firmus Technologies are the first named partners (together up to 210,000 GPUs).", "passages": ["Nvidia has announced a new business model under which it’ll be able to double-dip for revenue on the same silicon: once when its partner AI clouds use its hardware, and again as an ongoing percentage of the revenue that hardware generates. In a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress, the company pitched the “revenue-sharing and credit-support model” as a way to open compute access to startups that can’t finance it themselves.", "Under the structure, participating AI clouds procure Nvidia infrastructure and sell Nvidia-powered cloud services to end customers. Nvidia collects its usual product revenue on the hardware plus a percentage of the cloud income earned on that capacity, which the blog post describes as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream. Per Bloomberg , developers receive token credits in exchange for a slice of their future sales, but neither Nvidia nor its partners has disclosed the revenue-split percentages.", "Australia's Sharon AI and Singapore-based Firmus Technologies are the first named partners."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia has announced a new business model under which it’ll be able to double-dip for revenue on the same silicon: once when its partner AI clouds use its hardware, and again as an ongoing percentage of the revenue that hardware generates. In a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress, the company pitched the “revenue-sharing and credit-support model” as a way to open compute access to startups that can’t finance it themselves.", "Under the structure, participating AI clouds procure Nvidia infrastructure and sell Nvidia-powered cloud services to end customers. Nvidia collects its usual product revenue on the hardware plus a percentage of the cloud income earned on that capacity, which the blog post describes as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream. Per Bloomberg , developers receive token credits in exchange for a slice of their future sales, but neither Nvidia nor its partners has disclosed the revenue-split percentages.", "Australia's Sharon AI and Singapore-based Firmus Technologies are the first named partners."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Luke James, Tom's Hardware", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "28:e1", "article": 28, "input_id": "gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce", "title": "NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock", "publisher": "mitrade.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "NVIDIA unveiled a new AI compute framework under which cloud providers can deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements, aiming to lower infrastructure barriers for startups, enterprises, model developers and regional AI operators; NVIDIA earns revenue from hardware sales and from cloud usage generated by the supported capacity. NVIDIA's own post dated July 2, 2026 describes partnering with AI clouds to deploy large-scale, multi-tenant AI factories through revenue-sharing and credit support.", "passages": ["NVIDIA’s new AI compute framework allows cloud providers to deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements. The goal is to reduce infrastructure barriers for startups, enterprises, model developers, and regional AI operators.", "The company earns revenue from hardware sales and from cloud usage generated by supported capacity.", "NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories through revenue-sharing and credit-support."], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA’s new AI compute framework allows cloud providers to deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements. The goal is to reduce infrastructure barriers for startups, enterprises, model developers, and regional AI operators.", "The company earns revenue from hardware sales and from cloud usage generated by supported capacity.", "NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories through revenue-sharing and credit-support."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "mitrade.com, quoting NVIDIA's post of July 2, 2026", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-02", "statement_date_text": "July 2, 2026", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "38:e1", "article": 38, "input_id": "gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128", "title": "Nvidia Launches GPU Backstop Financing Model, Takes Cut of Cloud Revenue From Neocloud Partners", "publisher": "mlq.ai", "publication_date": "2026-07-03", "summary": "On July 1, 2026, Nvidia unveiled a financing vehicle it calls the \"AI Compute Partnership,\" under which it acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and in return takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate. Under the structure Nvidia guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs; if a partner's customer demand falls short, Nvidia commits to renting the idle capacity at a predetermined rate, absorbing downside risk that would otherwise sit with lenders or equity investors, and it collects standard product revenue plus a usage-linked cut of cloud revenue. Nvidia described the model in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress as providing \"economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\" The specific revenue-share percentage was not disclosed and Nvidia declined to offer further details beyond the blog post.", "passages": ["Nvidia on July 1 unveiled a new financing vehicle it calls the \"AI Compute Partnership,\" under which the chipmaker acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and, in return, takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate", "The backstop mechanism works by Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, effectively de-risking lender exposure and making it easier for smaller cloud operators to secure capital for large GPU deployments", "Under the AI Compute Partnership, Nvidia guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs. If a neocloud partner's customer demand falls short, Nvidia commits to renting the idle capacity at a predetermined rate, absorbing the downside risk that would otherwise sit with lenders or equity investors", "Nvidia described the model as providing \"economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model\" in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress", "The specific revenue-share percentage was not disclosed, and Nvidia declined to offer further details beyond the blog post"], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia on July 1 unveiled a new financing vehicle it calls the \"AI Compute Partnership,\" under which the chipmaker acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and, in return, takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate", "The backstop mechanism works by Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, effectively de-risking lender exposure and making it easier for smaller cloud operators to secure capital for large GPU deployments", "Under the AI Compute Partnership, Nvidia guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs. If a neocloud partner's customer demand falls short, Nvidia commits to renting the idle capacity at a predetermined rate, absorbing the downside risk that would otherwise sit with lenders or equity investors", "Nvidia described the model as providing \"economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model\" in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress", "The specific revenue-share percentage was not disclosed, and Nvidia declined to offer further details beyond the blog post"], "original_party": "Nvidia", "reporting_speaker": "mlq.ai", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "44:e1", "article": 44, "input_id": "gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4", "title": "Nvidia introduces revenue-sharing model for AI cloud financing", "publisher": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-04", "summary": "NVIDIA unveiled a revenue-sharing financing model under which AI cloud operators can procure NVIDIA infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold on that capacity; NVIDIA receives its standard product revenue from the infrastructure sale plus a share of the cloud revenue generated from the supported capacity. No dollar size or term for the credit support is disclosed.", "passages": ["Nvidia has unveiled a revenue-sharing financing model to assist AI cloud providers in acquiring its computing infrastructure, thereby enhancing access to large-scale AI compute for startups, enterprises, researchers, and regional providers.", "Under this financing structure, AI cloud operators can procure Nvidia infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold based on that capacity.", "Nvidia will receive its standard product revenue from infrastructure sales, in addition to a share of the cloud revenue generated from the supported capacity."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia has unveiled a revenue-sharing financing model to assist AI cloud providers in acquiring its computing infrastructure, thereby enhancing access to large-scale AI compute for startups, enterprises, researchers, and regional providers.", "Under this financing structure, AI cloud operators can procure Nvidia infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold based on that capacity.", "Nvidia will receive its standard product revenue from infrastructure sales, in addition to a share of the cloud revenue generated from the supported capacity."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "64:e1", "article": 64, "input_id": "gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57", "title": "NVIDIA DSX Promises More Revenue per Gigawatt. Who Actually Captures It?", "publisher": "futurumgroup.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "On July 1, 2026, NVIDIA introduced a business model under which AI cloud operators deploy large-scale, multi-tenant AI factories through a combination of revenue sharing and credit support, with the facilities built as DSX AI factories; participating clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered services, and NVIDIA earns its standard product revenue plus a share of the cloud revenue generated on the supported capacity. The item states NVIDIA has not disclosed the revenue-share percentage or how usage is measured.", "passages": ["The News: On July 1, 2026, NVIDIA introduced a business model that lets AI cloud operators deploy large-scale, multi-tenant AI factories through a combination of revenue sharing and credit support, with the resulting facilities built as DSX AI factories. Participating clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered services; NVIDIA earns its standard product revenue plus a share of the cloud revenue generated on the supported capacity.", "NVIDIA has not disclosed the revenue share percentage or how usage is measured."], "verified_passages": ["The News: On July 1, 2026, NVIDIA introduced a business model that lets AI cloud operators deploy large-scale, multi-tenant AI factories through a combination of revenue sharing and credit support, with the resulting facilities built as DSX AI factories. Participating clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered services; NVIDIA earns its standard product revenue plus a share of the cloud revenue generated on the supported capacity.", "NVIDIA has not disclosed the revenue share percentage or how usage is measured."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futurum Group", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1, 2026", "evidence_period": "Business model introduced July 1, 2026 (forward-looking arrangements)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "81:e1", "article": 81, "input_id": "gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677", "title": "Nvidia Corp. (NVDA) Announces a Profit-Sharing Program For Its Computing Framework Access", "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-07", "summary": "On July 1, 2026, NVIDIA disclosed a profit-sharing program that gives model builders, AI startups and businesses access to its computing framework without those entities having to fund hardware buildouts. Under the arrangement, NVIDIA will, in addition to product revenue, receive a share of cloud revenue based on the capacity it supports as AI cloud providers deliver NVIDIA-powered solutions to end users. CFO Colette Kress described the resulting income as a repeated, usage-based revenue stream that removes the need for location selection, building, energy procurement and hardware installation before accessing hyperscale computing.", "passages": ["On July 1, Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) disclosed a profit-sharing program developed to give model builders, AI startups, and businesses access to Nvidia's computing framework, without the need for these entities to fund hardware buildouts.", "Under this arrangement, NVIDIA, in addition to product revenue, will receive a share of cloud revenue based on the capacity it supports, as AI cloud providers deliver NVIDIA-powered solutions to their end users.", "In a blog post, the company's Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer, Colette Kress, defined income as a repeated, usage-based revenue stream, while noting that it eliminates the need for location selection, building, energy procurement, and hardware installation before accessing hyperscale computing."], "verified_passages": ["On July 1, Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) disclosed a profit-sharing program developed to give model builders, AI startups, and businesses access to Nvidia's computing framework, without the need for these entities to fund hardware buildouts.", "Under this arrangement, NVIDIA, in addition to product revenue, will receive a share of cloud revenue based on the capacity it supports, as AI cloud providers deliver NVIDIA-powered solutions to their end users.", "In a blog post, the company's Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer, Colette Kress, defined income as a repeated, usage-based revenue stream, while noting that it eliminates the need for location selection, building, energy procurement, and hardware installation before accessing hyperscale computing."], "original_party": "NVIDIA Corporation", "reporting_speaker": "finance.yahoo.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "108:e1", "article": 108, "input_id": "gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36", "title": "What's Up with NVIDIA's Latest Financial Model?", "publisher": "futuriom.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-08", "summary": "NVIDIA announced on July 1, 2026, a model under which it will guarantee the sale of GPU capacity for selected AI cloud providers (neoclouds) over several years and, in return, share in revenues those providers earn above the guaranteed, or backstop, level. In a joint announcement blog, NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri described it as a revenue-sharing and credit-support model under which AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services and NVIDIA earns both standard product revenue and a share of cloud revenue on the supported capacity. The item discloses no amount for the new guarantees.", "passages": ["NVIDIA shares tumbled on recent news that the vendor will guarantee the sale of GPU capacity for selected AI cloud providers (aka neoclouds) over several years. In return, NVIDIA will share in revenues earned above the guaranteed, or backstop, level.", "“This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of NVIDIA platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides NVIDIA with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream."], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA shares tumbled on recent news that the vendor will guarantee the sale of GPU capacity for selected AI cloud providers (aka neoclouds) over several years. In return, NVIDIA will share in revenues earned above the guaranteed, or backstop, level.", "“This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of NVIDIA platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides NVIDIA with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futuriom, reporting NVIDIA's announcement blog by CFO Colette Kress and VP Raj Mirpuri", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": "multi-year (several years from 2026)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v1": "1:e1", "v9": "1:e1", "v2": "16:e1", "v6": "18:e1"}, "revises": [{"group": "8:e2", "by": "18:e1"}]}, "1:e2": {"original": {"id": "1:e2", "article": 1, "input_id": "nvblog:nvidia-unlocks-ai-compute-at-scale-capital-partners-to-power-ai-infrastructure-buildout", "title": "NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog", "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Firmus Technologies is building a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which the company says is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs; the plan is disclosed in NVIDIA's announcement of its AI-cloud revenue-sharing and credit-support model. No timeline or contracted GPU volume is given.", "passages": ["Firmus is building a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia. The campus is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Firmus is building a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia. The campus is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "original_party": "Firmus Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "NVIDIA Corporation", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v2", "v22"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "8:e4", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Firmus, another first participant in the model, is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.", "passages": ["Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "original_party": "Firmus", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing NVIDIA press release)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "16:e3", "article": 16, "input_id": "gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5", "title": "Nvidia launches revenue-sharing model for AI startups", "publisher": "qz.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "NVIDIA named Firmus Technologies as an initial partner; a campus Firmus is developing in Batam, Indonesia is planned at a capacity of up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs and 360 megawatts of power.", "passages": ["A campus being developed by Firmus Technologies in Batam, Indonesia is planned at a capacity of up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs and 360 megawatts of power."], "verified_passages": ["A campus being developed by Firmus Technologies in Batam, Indonesia is planned at a capacity of up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs and 360 megawatts of power."], "original_party": "Firmus Technologies / NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "qz.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "17:e3", "article": 17, "input_id": "gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563", "title": "Nvidia taps AI cloud providers to expand compute access for startups", "publisher": "cnbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Firmus Technologies, an AI infrastructure company, is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs, as an initial partner in Nvidia's compute-access program.", "passages": ["Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs, while AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs, while AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "original_party": "Firmus Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "CNBC (citing Nvidia's announcement)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-02", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "18:e2", "article": 18, "input_id": "gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0", "title": "Nvidia acts as backstop for customer GPUs in return for cut of cloud revenue", "publisher": "datacenterdynamics.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia, and is one of the first companies to adopt Nvidia's revenue-sharing GPU rent-back backstop offer. The item does not specify the GPU generation or the deployment timing.", "passages": ["Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia"], "verified_passages": ["Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia"], "original_party": "Firmus", "reporting_speaker": "Georgia Butler, datacenterdynamics.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "21:e3", "article": 21, "input_id": "gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816", "title": "Nvidia offers to take a cut of AI cloud revenue on top of hardware sales in new optional financing vehicle — trades tokens for revenue cut", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Firmus Technologies is building a DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, that is expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.", "passages": ["Meanwhile, Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, that’s expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Meanwhile, Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, that’s expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "original_party": "Firmus Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "Luke James, Tom's Hardware", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "28:e3", "article": 28, "input_id": "gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce", "title": "NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock", "publisher": "mitrade.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "As another early participant in NVIDIA's new AI-factory compute programme, Firmus is developing a major campus in Indonesia that could support approximately 170,000 GPUs and 360 megawatts of power capacity.", "passages": ["Meanwhile, Firmus is developing a major campus in Indonesia that could support approximately 170,000 GPUs and 360 megawatts of power capacity."], "verified_passages": ["Meanwhile, Firmus is developing a major campus in Indonesia that could support approximately 170,000 GPUs and 360 megawatts of power capacity."], "original_party": "Firmus", "reporting_speaker": "mitrade.com", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "38:e3", "article": 38, "input_id": "gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128", "title": "Nvidia Launches GPU Backstop Financing Model, Takes Cut of Cloud Revenue From Neocloud Partners", "publisher": "mlq.ai", "publication_date": "2026-07-03", "summary": "Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications; the facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.", "passages": ["Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs"], "verified_passages": ["Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs"], "original_party": "Firmus Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "mlq.ai", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "44:e3", "article": 44, "input_id": "gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4", "title": "Nvidia introduces revenue-sharing model for AI cloud financing", "publisher": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-04", "summary": "Firmus is named as an early adopter of NVIDIA's revenue-sharing financing model and is developing a NVIDIA DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.", "passages": ["Two companies are among the first to collaborate with Nvidia under this model. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Two companies are among the first to collaborate with Nvidia under this model. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "original_party": "Firmus", "reporting_speaker": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "55:e6", "article": 55, "input_id": "gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6", "title": "Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters", "publisher": "newsletter.semianalysis.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Firmus announced on June 29, 2026 a 360MW AI cluster in Batam, Indonesia built with an Nvidia backstop, likely to be housed in a DayOne facility at Kabil Industrial Tech Park; Firmus expects $25-30 billion of customer revenue over the six years, with SemiAnalysis expecting a portion of revenue above the backstop level to be shared with Nvidia under the program structure.", "passages": ["Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.", "Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today."], "verified_passages": ["Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop. It will likely be housed in a DayOne facility in Kabil Industrial Tech Park (KITP). Announced just recently on June 29 th , 2026, this project shows the scale at which Nvidia is rolling out the backstop program.", "Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years. We expect a portion of the revenue above the backstop level will be shared with Nvidia as per the structure we outlined earlier today."], "original_party": "Firmus", "reporting_speaker": "SemiAnalysis", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-06-29", "statement_date_text": "June 29th, 2026", "evidence_period": "Six years from 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "64:e3", "article": 64, "input_id": "gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57", "title": "NVIDIA DSX Promises More Revenue per Gigawatt. Who Actually Captures It?", "publisher": "futurumgroup.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Firmus is among the first partners under NVIDIA's July 1, 2026 revenue-sharing and credit-support arrangement and is building a 360-megawatt DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 GPUs; it is co-designing its HyperCube architecture to NVIDIA's DSX blueprints and says the integration is meant to improve tokens per watt and cut cost per token for its customers.", "passages": ["Sharon AI, deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs across new capacity in Australia, and Firmus, building a 360-megawatt DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 GPUs, are among the first partners.", "Firmus is explicitly building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, co-designing its HyperCube architecture to NVIDIA’s DSX blueprints, and states the integration is meant to improve tokens per watt and reduce cost per token for its customers."], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI, deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs across new capacity in Australia, and Firmus, building a 360-megawatt DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 GPUs, are among the first partners.", "Firmus is explicitly building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, co-designing its HyperCube architecture to NVIDIA’s DSX blueprints, and states the integration is meant to improve tokens per watt and reduce cost per token for its customers."], "original_party": "Firmus / NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futurum Group", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1, 2026", "evidence_period": "Planned 360 MW campus targeting up to 170,000 GPUs, no completion date given", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "108:e3", "article": 108, "input_id": "gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36", "title": "What's Up with NVIDIA's Latest Financial Model?", "publisher": "futuriom.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-08", "summary": "Firmus, based in Indonesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs, as one of the two AI cloud providers NVIDIA said have signed on for its new revenue-sharing/credit-support model.", "passages": ["Firmus, based in Indoesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that’s expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Firmus, based in Indoesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that’s expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futuriom, reporting NVIDIA's announcement", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v1": "1:e2", "v2": "1:e2", "v22": "1:e2", "v20": "8:e4", "v9": "55:e6"}, "revises": []}, "2:e1": {"original": {"id": "2:e1", "article": 2, "input_id": "gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a", "title": "Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC", "publisher": "tradingkey.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "NVIDIA invested $5 billion of equity in Intel (NASDAQ: INTC), a transaction TradingKey's July 1, 2026 article treats as one of the two central catalysts of the Intel investment case and describes elsewhere as an equity commitment; the item gives no date for the investment itself.", "passages": ["Intel’s July investment thesis does not hinge on the Apple deal or Trump’s social media post, topics I’ve written about in the past few issues; rather, it turns on the fact that NVIDIA invested $5B into Intel as well as opted for Intel Xeon 6 as the host CPU in their DGX Rubin NVL8 AI systems.", "Add to the list of commitments NVIDIA's $5B equity commitment plus Xeon 6 product selection, Google's multi-year Xeon and custom ASIC deal, and Microsoft's previously confirmed 18A wafer deal, plus Apple foundry negotiations that are ongoing.", "The Intel story now includes a $5 billion equity investment from NVIDIA for Xeon 6 as the host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8, a Google multiyear agreement with locked volume and pricing (3-to-5-year deployment and co-development of Intel custom AI accelerators (ASIC)), and Microsoft has signed a deal for wafers using 18A technology."], "verified_passages": ["Intel’s July investment thesis does not hinge on the Apple deal or Trump’s social media post, topics I’ve written about in the past few issues; rather, it turns on the fact that NVIDIA invested $5B into Intel as well as opted for Intel Xeon 6 as the host CPU in their DGX Rubin NVL8 AI systems.", "Add to the list of commitments NVIDIA's $5B equity commitment plus Xeon 6 product selection, Google's multi-year Xeon and custom ASIC deal, and Microsoft's previously confirmed 18A wafer deal, plus Apple foundry negotiations that are ongoing.", "The Intel story now includes a $5 billion equity investment from NVIDIA for Xeon 6 as the host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8, a Google multiyear agreement with locked volume and pricing (3-to-5-year deployment and co-development of Intel custom AI accelerators (ASIC)), and Microsoft has signed a deal for wafers using 18A technology."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "TradingKey", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [{"measure": "equity investment in Intel", "period": null, "value": "$5B", "kind": "actual", "basis": "equity investment (also described as an equity commitment) by NVIDIA in Intel"}], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v9": "2:e1"}, "revises": []}, "2:e2": {"original": {"id": "2:e2", "article": 2, "input_id": "gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a", "title": "Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC", "publisher": "tradingkey.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "NVIDIA selected Intel's Xeon 6 as the host CPU for its DGX Rubin NVL8 AI systems, a product-architecture decision reported by TradingKey on July 1, 2026; the article describes the DGX Rubin NVL8 as the AI system intended to power data centres over the next two to three years and for the next product cycle, but gives no shipment timing or unit volumes.", "passages": ["NVIDIA could have gone with any CPU to accompany their Rubin GPU, but they went with Intel Xeon 6 to power the DGX Rubin NVL8, the AI system that will power the data centre for the next two to three years.", "NVIDIA allocated $5B of equity to Intel and chose Intel's Xeon 6 as the host CPU for its DGX Rubin NVL8 AI systems, the AI product to set the benchmark for data centre AI systems for the next product cycle?", "NVIDIA selection: Xeon 6 chosen as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8; $5B equity investment"], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA could have gone with any CPU to accompany their Rubin GPU, but they went with Intel Xeon 6 to power the DGX Rubin NVL8, the AI system that will power the data centre for the next two to three years.", "NVIDIA allocated $5B of equity to Intel and chose Intel's Xeon 6 as the host CPU for its DGX Rubin NVL8 AI systems, the AI product to set the benchmark for data centre AI systems for the next product cycle?", "NVIDIA selection: Xeon 6 chosen as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8; $5B equity investment"], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "TradingKey", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Rubin product cycle; article describes the DGX Rubin NVL8 as powering data centres for the next two to three years", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v19", "v20", "v7"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v19": "2:e2", "v20": "2:e2", "v7": "2:e2"}, "revises": []}, "2:e3": {"original": {"id": "2:e3", "article": 2, "input_id": "gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a", "title": "Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC", "publisher": "tradingkey.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan said recently that the CPU has become the orchestration layer and control plane of AI infrastructure and that, in inference workloads, the CPU-to-GPU ratio is shifting from 1 CPU to 8 GPUs toward 1 CPU to 1 GPU, meaning the number of CPUs needed to support each GPU is rising; the item gives no date beyond 'recently' and cites no data behind the ratio.", "passages": ["CEO Lip-Bu Tan recently said Xeon 6 now plays the role of “the orchestration layer and critical control plane for the entire AI stack” and highlighted that the CPU:GPU ratio for inference is beginning to shift from 1-to-8 to 1:1, meaning the ratio of CPUs needed to support the GPU is actually increasing, not decreasing (the prior narrative was that GPUs would ultimately take over the CPU role).", "Here's the explanation from Lip-Bu Tan: \"The CPU has become the orchestration layer, the control plane of the entire AI infrastructure. In inference workloads, we're starting to shift from 1 CPU to 8 GPUs towards 1 CPU to 1 GPU.\""], "verified_passages": ["CEO Lip-Bu Tan recently said Xeon 6 now plays the role of “the orchestration layer and critical control plane for the entire AI stack” and highlighted that the CPU:GPU ratio for inference is beginning to shift from 1-to-8 to 1:1, meaning the ratio of CPUs needed to support the GPU is actually increasing, not decreasing (the prior narrative was that GPUs would ultimately take over the CPU role).", "Here's the explanation from Lip-Bu Tan: \"The CPU has become the orchestration layer, the control plane of the entire AI infrastructure. In inference workloads, we're starting to shift from 1 CPU to 8 GPUs towards 1 CPU to 1 GPU.\""], "original_party": "Lip-Bu Tan, CEO of Intel", "reporting_speaker": "TradingKey", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "recently", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v19"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v19": "2:e3"}, "revises": []}, "2:e4": {"original": {"id": "2:e4", "article": 2, "input_id": "gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a", "title": "Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC", "publisher": "tradingkey.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Google signed a multiyear deal, announced with its Q1 2026 results, to keep using Intel Xeon processors in its workload-optimized instances, including Xeon 6 in its C4 and N4 instances, and is co-developing custom ASIC Infrastructure Processing Unit (IPU) chips with Intel; Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan said the agreements span three to five years with locked volume and pricing. The article elsewhere calls the co-developed chips 'custom AI accelerators (ASIC)', while the deal description specifies IPUs.", "passages": ["Google inked a multiyear deal for continued use of Intel Xeon processors in Google's workload-optimized instances, including the newest Xeon 6 processors that power C4 and N4 instances. The companies also are partnering on custom-designed ASIC Infrastructure Processing Unit (IPU) chips that will help boost utilization, lower system complexity, and scale more efficiently for AI tasks.", "CEO Tan said the agreements span three to five years, with locked volume and pricing.", "a Google multiyear agreement with locked volume and pricing (3-to-5-year deployment and co-development of Intel custom AI accelerators (ASIC))"], "verified_passages": ["Google inked a multiyear deal for continued use of Intel Xeon processors in Google's workload-optimized instances, including the newest Xeon 6 processors that power C4 and N4 instances. The companies also are partnering on custom-designed ASIC Infrastructure Processing Unit (IPU) chips that will help boost utilization, lower system complexity, and scale more efficiently for AI tasks.", "CEO Tan said the agreements span three to five years, with locked volume and pricing.", "a Google multiyear agreement with locked volume and pricing (3-to-5-year deployment and co-development of Intel custom AI accelerators (ASIC))"], "original_party": "Google and Intel", "reporting_speaker": "TradingKey", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "Q1 2026", "evidence_period": "three to five years (deal term)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v16", "v19"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v16": "2:e4", "v19": "2:e4"}, "revises": []}, "4:e1": {"original": {"id": "4:e1", "article": 4, "input_id": "gnews:8f5a03f1dde395491fc3814b", "title": "Anthropic, NVIDIA Move AI Agents Deeper into Scientific Workflows", "publisher": "campustechnology.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "NVIDIA announced the BioNeMo Agent Toolkit on June 23, 2026 — a set of domain-specific tools and skills for agentic life-sciences workflows, encompassing NVIDIA life-sciences libraries, tools and open models, designed to help agents gather evidence, reason across findings, run computational experiments and recommend next steps.", "passages": ["NVIDIA's role comes through its BioNeMo Agent Toolkit , which the chipmaker announced June 23.", "NVIDIA describes BioNeMo Agent Toolkit as a set of domain-specific tools and skills for agentic life sciences workflows. The toolkit includes NVIDIA life sciences libraries, tools, and open models, and is designed to help agents gather evidence, reason across findings, run computational experiments, and recommend next steps."], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA's role comes through its BioNeMo Agent Toolkit , which the chipmaker announced June 23.", "NVIDIA describes BioNeMo Agent Toolkit as a set of domain-specific tools and skills for agentic life sciences workflows. The toolkit includes NVIDIA life sciences libraries, tools, and open models, and is designed to help agents gather evidence, reason across findings, run computational experiments, and recommend next steps."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "John K. Waters, campustechnology.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-06-23", "statement_date_text": "June 23", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "236:e1", "article": 236, "input_id": "gnews:b46d410f1a3e3ad1888d51de", "title": "How Tecan uses NVIDIA’s BioNeMo Agent Toolkit to flag lab risks before runs fail", "publisher": "rdworldonline.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-14", "summary": "NVIDIA released its BioNeMo Agent Toolkit in late June 2026; the toolkit packages NVIDIA's life-science models and libraries as tools an AI agent can call, and NVIDIA has promoted it largely for scientific work such as protein structure prediction, molecular docking, generative chemistry and genomic analysis.", "passages": ["In late June, NVIDIA released the BioNeMo Agent Toolkit , which packages the company’s life-science models and libraries as tools an AI agent can call.", "NVIDIA has promoted it largely for scientific work such as protein structure prediction, molecular docking, generative chemistry and genomic analysis."], "verified_passages": ["In late June, NVIDIA released the BioNeMo Agent Toolkit , which packages the company’s life-science models and libraries as tools an AI agent can call.", "NVIDIA has promoted it largely for scientific work such as protein structure prediction, molecular docking, generative chemistry and genomic analysis."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Brian Buntz, R&D World (rdworldonline.com)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "late June 2026", "evidence_period": "late June 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "4:e2": {"original": {"id": "4:e2", "article": 4, "input_id": "gnews:8f5a03f1dde395491fc3814b", "title": "Anthropic, NVIDIA Move AI Agents Deeper into Scientific Workflows", "publisher": "campustechnology.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Anthropic introduced Claude Science (beta), announced June 30, 2026, an AI research workbench for scientists available on macOS and Linux for Claude Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise users; Anthropic said it uses NVIDIA's BioNeMo Agent Toolkit skills to connect to life-sciences models and libraries in BioNeMo, including Evo 2, Boltz-2 and OpenFold3.", "passages": ["The beta release, announced June 30, gives Claude Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise users access to an application designed to help researchers work across literature review, data analysis, figure generation, manuscript refinement, and computational workflows.", "Anthropic said Claude Science uses BioNeMo Agent Toolkit skills to connect to life sciences models and libraries in BioNeMo, including Evo 2, Boltz-2, and OpenFold3."], "verified_passages": ["The beta release, announced June 30, gives Claude Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise users access to an application designed to help researchers work across literature review, data analysis, figure generation, manuscript refinement, and computational workflows.", "Anthropic said Claude Science uses BioNeMo Agent Toolkit skills to connect to life sciences models and libraries in BioNeMo, including Evo 2, Boltz-2, and OpenFold3."], "original_party": "Anthropic", "reporting_speaker": "John K. Waters, campustechnology.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-06-30", "statement_date_text": "June 30", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "5:e1": {"original": {"id": "5:e1", "article": 5, "input_id": "gnews:ad47330f25c9d5ff84ced7e2", "title": "Valar Atomics wants to power data center using minimal water", "publisher": "deseret.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Valar Atomics announced a collaboration with Nvidia to explore AI data centers powered directly by advanced nuclear energy, which the item calls a first for the industry. The companies are considering a proposed 30-megawatt, nearly waterless data center in Utah that would use Valar's Ward250 reactor together with Nvidia's water-efficient cooling technology; the item describes the project as conditional ('if the collaboration proceeds') and as under exploration, not a committed order or deployment.", "passages": ["Valar Atomics announced a partnership with Nvidia to explore AI data centers powered directly by advanced nuclear energy, marking a first for the industry.", "The companies are considering a 30-megawatt, nearly waterless data center in Utah using Valar’s Ward250 reactor and Nvidia’s water-efficient cooling technology."], "verified_passages": ["Valar Atomics announced a partnership with Nvidia to explore AI data centers powered directly by advanced nuclear energy, marking a first for the industry.", "The companies are considering a 30-megawatt, nearly waterless data center in Utah using Valar’s Ward250 reactor and Nvidia’s water-efficient cooling technology."], "original_party": "Valar Atomics and Nvidia", "reporting_speaker": "Deseret News (Eva Terry)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "Wednesday afternoon", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "26:e1", "article": 26, "input_id": "gnews:b680fbe2c3e9228eba33a0b4", "title": "Startup activates nuclear microreactor live on stage to power an Nvidia RTX Spark desktop PC — firm working with Nvidia to build a 30MW closed loop AI factory that doesn’t use local water", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Valar Atomics announced a partnership with Nvidia to power an AI factory, described in the article's headline as a 30MW closed-loop AI factory that does not use local water; the announcement came at a live event where Valar activated its Ward 250 nuclear microreactor on stage. No contract value, equipment volume, site, timing or Nvidia confirmation is given.", "passages": ["Startup activates nuclear microreactor live on stage to power an Nvidia RTX Spark desktop PC — firm working with Nvidia to build a 30MW closed loop AI factory that doesn't use local water", "Valar Atomics activated its Ward 250 nuclear microreactor on stage during a live event, where it announced its partnership with Nvidia to power an AI factory."], "verified_passages": ["Startup activates nuclear microreactor live on stage to power an Nvidia RTX Spark desktop PC — firm working with Nvidia to build a 30MW closed loop AI factory that doesn’t use local water", "Valar Atomics activated its Ward 250 nuclear microreactor on stage during a live event, where it announced its partnership with Nvidia to power an AI factory."], "original_party": "Valar Atomics", "reporting_speaker": "Jowi Morales (Tom's Hardware)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "67:e2", "article": 67, "input_id": "gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb", "title": "A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water", "publisher": "autonocion.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Alongside the demonstration, Nvidia and Valar Atomics announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems; the concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah that Valar's announcement says consumes no water from the local community. Nvidia global vice president John Josephakis told Reuters the company is 'exploring' how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories. No construction schedule, investment figure, or permit has been published.", "passages": ["Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”", "“Through this work with Valar Atomics, Nvidia is exploring how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories,” John Josephakis, a global vice president at Nvidia, told Reuters.", "What nobody has published is a construction schedule, an investment figure, or a permit."], "verified_passages": ["Alongside the demo, the two companies announced an agreement to jointly explore nuclear-powered AI systems. The concrete version under study is a 30-megawatt closed-loop AI factory in Utah, which Valar’s own announcement says “consumes no water from the local community.”", "“Through this work with Valar Atomics, Nvidia is exploring how behind-the-meter, waterless advanced nuclear systems could support future AI factories,” John Josephakis, a global vice president at Nvidia, told Reuters.", "What nobody has published is a construction schedule, an investment figure, or a permit."], "original_party": "Nvidia and Valar Atomics", "reporting_speaker": "autonocion.com, quoting Reuters and Valar/Nvidia statements", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["clean-2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"clean-2": "67:e2"}, "revises": []}, "5:e2": {"original": {"id": "5:e2", "article": 5, "input_id": "gnews:ad47330f25c9d5ff84ced7e2", "title": "Valar Atomics wants to power data center using minimal water", "publisher": "deseret.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Nvidia announced a new AI factory design, DSX, that uses a highly water-efficient direct liquid cooling system in which water pumped through the factory remains at 113°F, eliminating the need for power-hungry water chillers. The item presents this as a recently made product-design announcement by Nvidia and does not give a date, deployment volume or financial figure.", "passages": ["Nvidia recently announced its new AI factory design, DSX, which uses a highly water-efficient direct liquid cooling system. Water pumped through the factory remains at 113°F to eliminate the need for power-hungry water chillers."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia recently announced its new AI factory design, DSX, which uses a highly water-efficient direct liquid cooling system. Water pumped through the factory remains at 113°F to eliminate the need for power-hungry water chillers."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Deseret News (Eva Terry)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "recently", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "6:e1": {"original": {"id": "6:e1", "article": 6, "input_id": "gnews:c3c81e4fb573a723e4081dd0", "title": "One of America's oldest manufacturers says AI is creating jobs — not replacing them", "publisher": "foxnews.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Wistron, a Taiwan-based electronics manufacturer, is establishing AI supercomputer manufacturing operations in Texas for NVIDIA, according to Fox News, which reported the move as bringing advanced manufacturing jobs to the state. Wistron Chairman Simon Lin is quoted saying that building in America is essential for speed, resilience and strategic advantage, and that Texas offers talent, industrial strength and strategic location to support the next generation of AI infrastructure. No capacity, investment amount, product generation or start date was disclosed.", "passages": ["Wistron, a Taiwan-based electronics manufacturer, is establishing AI supercomputer manufacturing operations in Texas for NVIDIA, bringing advanced manufacturing jobs to the state.", "\"Building in America is essential for speed, resilience and strategic advantage,\" Wistron Chairman Simon Lin told Fox News Digital.", "\"Texas offers the talent, industrial strength, and strategic location to help power the next generation of AI infrastructure, while creating durable, high-value jobs at scale for the local workforce,\" he added."], "verified_passages": ["Wistron, a Taiwan-based electronics manufacturer, is establishing AI supercomputer manufacturing operations in Texas for NVIDIA, bringing advanced manufacturing jobs to the state.", "\"Building in America is essential for speed, resilience and strategic advantage,\" Wistron Chairman Simon Lin told Fox News Digital.", "\"Texas offers the talent, industrial strength, and strategic location to help power the next generation of AI infrastructure, while creating durable, high-value jobs at scale for the local workforce,\" he added."], "original_party": "Wistron", "reporting_speaker": "Fox News (Amanda Macias)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "7:e1": {"original": {"id": "7:e1", "article": 7, "input_id": "gnews:9a13ec8bfdc32e585c1f0604", "title": "Why NN (NNBR) Is Up 24.7% After Pre-Selling New NVIDIA Liquid Cooling Capacity Expansion", "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "NN, Inc. (NNBR) announced in late June 2026 a major expansion of its liquid cooling production for NVIDIA AI data center racks, adding 47 new machine centers at its Wuxi, China plant, with 100% of the new capacity already pre-sold and tied to multi-year, multi-product awards. The company said the move deepens its role in NVIDIA's Asia supply chain (while repurposing legacy automotive capacity) and that it targets US$80–US$90 million of accretive new business in 2026.", "passages": ["In late June 2026, NN, Inc. announced a major expansion of its liquid cooling production for NVIDIA AI data center racks, adding 47 new machine centers in its Wuxi, China plant with 100% of this new capacity already pre-sold and tied to multi-year, multi-product awards.", "This move effectively deepens NN's role in NVIDIA's Asia supply chain while repurposing legacy automotive capacity and targeting US$80–US$90 million of accretive new business in 2026."], "verified_passages": ["In late June 2026, NN, Inc. announced a major expansion of its liquid cooling production for NVIDIA AI data center racks, adding 47 new machine centers in its Wuxi, China plant with 100% of this new capacity already pre-sold and tied to multi-year, multi-product awards.", "This move effectively deepens NN's role in NVIDIA's Asia supply chain while repurposing legacy automotive capacity and targeting US$80–US$90 million of accretive new business in 2026."], "original_party": "NN, Inc.", "reporting_speaker": "finance.yahoo.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "late June 2026", "evidence_period": "2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v2": "7:e1", "v20": "7:e1"}, "revises": []}, "8:e2": {"original": {"id": "8:e2", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "The Information reported that NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs: if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price; in return NVIDIA will receive a percentage of the providers' revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the contract term. GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.", "passages": ["On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price. In return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract. GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement."], "verified_passages": ["On July 1, according to the technology news outlet The Information, NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs—if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price.\nIn return, NVIDIA will receive a percentage of these cloud providers’ revenue, with the revenue-sharing rate gradually declining over the term of the contract. GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement."], "original_party": "The Information", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing The Information; arrangement attributed to unnamed executives)", "tier": "rumour", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "55:e4", "article": 55, "input_id": "gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6", "title": "Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters", "publisher": "newsletter.semianalysis.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "SemiAnalysis said Nvidia's backstop program is typically six years in length, with Nvidia standing ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the term and terms negotiated individually by each neocloud; in an illustrative backstop pricing curve the authors believe sits at the low end of the range, the backstop averages $2.36 per GPU-hour over the six years, and they expect most neoclouds to negotiate higher backstops.", "passages": ["Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period. Each Neocloud is expected to negotiate the backstop terms individually, and we can expect that different Neoclouds may end up with different revenue share and backstop schedules. The below table is an illustrative example to explain the basic terms of the program – we present a backstop pricing curve that we believe to be on the lower end of the backstop range – in this case at an average of $2.36 over the six-year period, but we expect that most Neoclouds will negotiate higher backstops."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia’s backstop program is typically six years in length, and during these six years, Nvidia stands ready to purchase compute at pre-agreed price levels that vary over the time period. Each Neocloud is expected to negotiate the backstop terms individually, and we can expect that different Neoclouds may end up with different revenue share and backstop schedules. The below table is an illustrative example to explain the basic terms of the program – we present a backstop pricing curve that we believe to be on the lower end of the backstop range – in this case at an average of $2.36 over the six-year period, but we expect that most Neoclouds will negotiate higher backstops."], "original_party": "Nvidia", "reporting_speaker": "SemiAnalysis", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": "2026-07-06", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Six years per backstop, from 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v9": "8:e2"}, "revises": []}, "8:e3": {"original": {"id": "8:e3", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Sharon AI, one of the first cloud providers participating in NVIDIA's new model, plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.", "passages": ["Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs,"], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs,"], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing NVIDIA press release)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "16:e2", "article": 16, "input_id": "gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5", "title": "Nvidia launches revenue-sharing model for AI startups", "publisher": "qz.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "NVIDIA named Sharon AI as one of two initial partners in its revenue-sharing/compute-access program; Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.", "passages": ["Nvidia named two initial partners. Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia named two initial partners. Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "original_party": "NVIDIA / Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "qz.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "17:e2", "article": 17, "input_id": "gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563", "title": "Nvidia taps AI cloud providers to expand compute access for startups", "publisher": "cnbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Sharon AI, an Australian AI cloud provider named as an initial partner in Nvidia's new compute-access program, will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs.", "passages": ["Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs, while AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs, while AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "CNBC (citing Nvidia's announcement)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-02", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "18:e3", "article": 18, "input_id": "gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0", "title": "Nvidia acts as backstop for customer GPUs in return for cut of cloud revenue", "publisher": "datacenterdynamics.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs and is one of the first companies to adopt Nvidia's revenue-sharing GPU rent-back backstop offer.", "passages": ["Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs"], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs"], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "Georgia Butler, datacenterdynamics.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "21:e2", "article": 21, "input_id": "gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816", "title": "Nvidia offers to take a cut of AI cloud revenue on top of hardware sales in new optional financing vehicle — trades tokens for revenue cut", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Sharon AI disclosed in an 8-K filing dated June 12 that its agreement with NVIDIA under the new model runs for six years and covers 72 MW of new Australian data center capacity built to NVIDIA's DSX AI factory design, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.", "passages": ["In an 8-K filing dated June 12th, Sharon AI disclosed that the agreement runs for six years and covers 72 MW of new Australian data center capacity built to Nvidia's DSX AI factory design, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["In an 8-K filing dated June 12th, Sharon AI disclosed that the agreement runs for six years and covers 72 MW of new Australian data center capacity built to Nvidia's DSX AI factory design, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "Luke James, Tom's Hardware", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-06-12", "statement_date_text": "June 12th", "evidence_period": "Six-year agreement term (from June 2026)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "28:e2", "article": 28, "input_id": "gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce", "title": "NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock", "publisher": "mitrade.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "As an early participant in NVIDIA's new AI-factory compute programme, Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.", "passages": ["Early participants illustrate the scale of the initiative. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Early participants illustrate the scale of the initiative. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs."], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "mitrade.com", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "38:e2", "article": 38, "input_id": "gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128", "title": "Nvidia Launches GPU Backstop Financing Model, Takes Cut of Cloud Revenue From Neocloud Partners", "publisher": "mlq.ai", "publication_date": "2026-07-03", "summary": "Sharon AI (NASDAQ: SHAZ), an Australian sovereign-cloud provider, plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs in Australia under a six-year agreement with Nvidia. It listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO and raised an additional $1.6 billion in a June 2026 private placement to fund its Nvidia-based AI factory.", "passages": ["Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia", "The company raised an additional $1.6 billion in private placement in June 2026 to fund its Nvidia-based AI factory"], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia", "The company raised an additional $1.6 billion in private placement in June 2026 to fund its Nvidia-based AI factory"], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "mlq.ai", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "six-year agreement", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "44:e2", "article": 44, "input_id": "gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4", "title": "Nvidia introduces revenue-sharing model for AI cloud financing", "publisher": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-04", "summary": "Sharon AI is named as an early adopter of NVIDIA's revenue-sharing financing model and plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under it.", "passages": ["Two companies are among the first to collaborate with Nvidia under this model. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "verified_passages": ["Two companies are among the first to collaborate with Nvidia under this model. Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, while Firmus is developing a DSX AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs."], "original_party": "Sharon AI", "reporting_speaker": "datacenters.economictimes.indiatimes.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "55:e5", "article": 55, "input_id": "gnews:085b1e1a1543437edb9756d6", "title": "Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters", "publisher": "newsletter.semianalysis.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "SharonAI's 72MW AI factory in Australia, announced in June 2026, scales to as many as 40,000 GB300 GPUs under a six-year Nvidia backstop; SharonAI disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88 billion, an implied floor of about $2.33 per GPU-hour on average over the six years, and guides to more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total by mid-2027 as its footprint grows to 132MW, of which 102MW is contracted.", "passages": ["The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027."], "verified_passages": ["The first is SharonAI’s 72MW AI factory in Australia. Announced in June 2026, the deal has SharonAI scaling up to as many as 40,000 GB300s under a six-year backstop. Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B, which works out to an implied floor of about $2.33/hr/GPU on average over the six year period. Sharon AI’s footprint is now set to grow to 132MW with 102MW contracted, and the company guides to reaching more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs in total (inclusive of the 40,000 GB300s backstopped) by mid-2027."], "original_party": "SharonAI", "reporting_speaker": "SemiAnalysis", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "June 2026", "evidence_period": "Six-year backstop from 2026; more than 55,000 Nvidia GPUs by mid-2027", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "64:e2", "article": 64, "input_id": "gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57", "title": "NVIDIA DSX Promises More Revenue per Gigawatt. Who Actually Captures It?", "publisher": "futurumgroup.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Sharon AI is among the first partners under NVIDIA's July 1, 2026 revenue-sharing and credit-support arrangement and is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs across new capacity in Australia, according to the Futurum Group's account of the announcement. The figure is a stated deployment plan, not a confirmed order or shipment.", "passages": ["Sharon AI, deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs across new capacity in Australia, and Firmus, building a 360-megawatt DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 GPUs, are among the first partners."], "verified_passages": ["Sharon AI, deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs across new capacity in Australia, and Firmus, building a 360-megawatt DSX-aligned AI factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 GPUs, are among the first partners."], "original_party": "Sharon AI / NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futurum Group", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1, 2026", "evidence_period": "Planned new capacity in Australia (up to 40,000 GB300 GPUs), no delivery date given", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "108:e2", "article": 108, "input_id": "gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36", "title": "What's Up with NVIDIA's Latest Financial Model?", "publisher": "futuriom.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-08", "summary": "NVIDIA stated that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for its new revenue-sharing/credit-support model, and that Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan.", "passages": ["NVIDIA states that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for the new deal: Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan."], "verified_passages": ["NVIDIA states that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for the new deal: Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Futuriom, reporting NVIDIA's announcement", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20", "v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v20": "8:e3", "v1": "16:e2", "v2": "16:e2", "v9": "55:e5"}, "revises": [{"group": "8:e2", "by": "108:e2"}]}, "8:e5": {"original": {"id": "8:e5", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "According to a regulatory filing NVIDIA submitted in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.", "passages": ["According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares."], "verified_passages": ["According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing NVIDIA regulatory filing)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "May of this year", "evidence_period": "quarter ended April 2026", "figures": [{"measure": "added guarantee for customer data center leases", "period": "quarter ended April 2026", "value": "$3.5 billion", "kind": "actual", "basis": "guarantees of customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase the customers' shares"}], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v9": "8:e5"}, "revises": []}, "8:e6": {"original": {"id": "8:e6", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "In September 2024, NVIDIA committed to purchasing all of CoreWeave's unsold capacity through 2032 if CoreWeave failed to secure tenants, under a contract then valued at $6.3 billion.", "passages": ["In September 2024, NVIDIA committed to purchasing all of CoreWeave’s unsold capacity through 2032 if CoreWeave failed to secure tenants, under a contract then valued at $6.3 billion."], "verified_passages": ["In September 2024, NVIDIA committed to purchasing all of CoreWeave’s unsold capacity through 2032 if CoreWeave failed to secure tenants, under a contract then valued at $6.3 billion."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "September 2024", "evidence_period": "through 2032", "figures": [{"measure": "commitment to purchase CoreWeave's unsold capacity (contract value)", "period": "through 2032", "value": "$6.3 billion", "kind": "actual", "basis": "contingent on CoreWeave failing to secure tenants"}], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v9": "8:e6"}, "revises": []}, "8:e7": {"original": {"id": "8:e7", "article": 8, "input_id": "gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45", "title": "NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.", "publisher": "moomoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI's lease of a large data center in Ohio, an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion. The $500 billion is the estimated asset cost, not a stated size of NVIDIA's guarantee; the negotiation is unconfirmed.", "passages": ["According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion."], "verified_passages": ["According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion."], "original_party": "The Information", "reporting_speaker": "moomoo.com (citing prior reporting by The Information)", "tier": "rumour", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v9": "8:e7"}, "revises": []}, "10:e1": {"original": {"id": "10:e1", "article": 10, "input_id": "gnews:4f3a1d09e90b8fec9c86d2ba", "title": "Nvidia RTX 5090 GPUs are so expensive that Intel's Arc Pro B70 is now a genuine bargain for AI — 128GB 4-card configuration costs less than $3800", "publisher": "techradar.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "TechRadar's Rahim Amir reported that Nvidia's RTX 5090 — a consumer GPU with 32GB of GDDR7 memory and a launch MSRP of $2,000 for the Founders Edition — was selling in 2026 for as much as two times that stated MSRP, leading many cost-sensitive local-AI builders to buy older 24GB Nvidia GPUs (RTX 4090, 3090 Ti, 3090) instead. The tier reflects the outlet's own observation of market prices, not a company-disclosed figure.", "passages": ["Nvidia 's RTX 5090 is a uniquely capable GPU - the company's highest-end consumer-grade GPU to date features a whopping 21,760 CUDA cores and 32GB of GDDR7 memory in its cut-down GB202 configuration.", "It also happens to be one of the most expensive GPUs retail consumers can buy in 2026, going for as much as two times its stated MSRP of $2,000 for the Founders Edition at launch, leaving many cost-sensitive AI builders turning to older Nvidia GPUs equipped with 24GB of VRAM such as the RTX 4090, 3090Ti and 3090."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia 's RTX 5090 is a uniquely capable GPU - the company's highest-end consumer-grade GPU to date features a whopping 21,760 CUDA cores and 32GB of GDDR7 memory in its cut-down GB202 configuration.", "It also happens to be one of the most expensive GPUs retail consumers can buy in 2026, going for as much as two times its stated MSRP of $2,000 for the Founders Edition at launch, leaving many cost-sensitive AI builders turning to older Nvidia GPUs equipped with 24GB of VRAM such as the RTX 4090, 3090Ti and 3090."], "original_party": "TechRadar (Rahim Amir), reporting Nvidia product pricing", "reporting_speaker": "Rahim Amir, TechRadar", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "10:e2": {"original": {"id": "10:e2", "article": 10, "input_id": "gnews:4f3a1d09e90b8fec9c86d2ba", "title": "Nvidia RTX 5090 GPUs are so expensive that Intel's Arc Pro B70 is now a genuine bargain for AI — 128GB 4-card configuration costs less than $3800", "publisher": "techradar.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Intel's highest-end Arc Pro workstation GPU, the Arc Pro B70, carries a reference price of $950, with most retailers and OEM partners selling SKUs at around $1,000 for a 32GB GDDR6 card built on Intel's BMG-G31 \"Big Battlemage\" chip; the article states this is effectively a quarter of most RTX 5090 prices then on sale and positions the card as a value alternative to Nvidia for local AI workloads. Nvidia is said to retain an advantage through CUDA software support.", "passages": ["The Intel Arc Pro B70 is its highest-end offering and commands a reference price of $950, with most retailers and OEM partners selling SKUs at around $1,000.", "With 32GB of GDDR6 memory in tow and a price that is effectively a quarter of most RTX 5090 SKUs on sale at the time of writing, it holds its own as a value-centric alternative to Nvidia's Blackwell-based behemoth.", "It leverages Intel's BMG-G31 \"Big Battlemage\" chip that was originally slated to show on its since-canceled Arc B770 GPU , as it aims to address a vacuum in the local AI space that both AMD and Nvidia are not willing to address given their focus on maximizing profits at the highest end of the spectrum with enterprise consumers."], "verified_passages": ["The Intel Arc Pro B70 is its highest-end offering and commands a reference price of $950, with most retailers and OEM partners selling SKUs at around $1,000.", "With 32GB of GDDR6 memory in tow and a price that is effectively a quarter of most RTX 5090 SKUs on sale at the time of writing, it holds its own as a value-centric alternative to Nvidia's Blackwell-based behemoth.", "It leverages Intel's BMG-G31 \"Big Battlemage\" chip that was originally slated to show on its since-canceled Arc B770 GPU , as it aims to address a vacuum in the local AI space that both AMD and Nvidia are not willing to address given their focus on maximizing profits at the highest end of the spectrum with enterprise consumers."], "original_party": "Intel (product reference pricing)", "reporting_speaker": "Rahim Amir, TechRadar", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "11:e1": {"original": {"id": "11:e1", "article": 11, "input_id": "gnews:87742e41d1edc4e292c234fe", "title": "Alex Karp Touts Palantir-Nvidia Partnership For Secure AI, Criticizes OpenAI And Anthropic Over Lack Of IP Protection", "publisher": "es.tradingview.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Palantir Technologies announced earlier this week that it is integrating Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models into its new intelligent engine to deliver mission-specific sovereign AI for U.S. government agencies and critical infrastructure operators; Palantir said the system lets organizations deploy frontier-level AI in secure, air-gapped environments while keeping sensitive data off public networks.", "passages": ["Palantir announced earlier this week that it is integrating Nvidia’s Nemotron open AI models into its new intelligent engine to deliver mission-specific sovereign AI for U.S. government agencies and critical infrastructure operators. The company said the system enables organizations to deploy frontier-level AI in secure, air-gapped environments while keeping sensitive data off public networks."], "verified_passages": ["Palantir announced earlier this week that it is integrating Nvidia’s Nemotron open AI models into its new intelligent engine to deliver mission-specific sovereign AI for U.S. government agencies and critical infrastructure operators. The company said the system enables organizations to deploy frontier-level AI in secure, air-gapped environments while keeping sensitive data off public networks."], "original_party": "Palantir Technologies Inc.", "reporting_speaker": "TradingView (Stocktwits), reporting Palantir's announcement", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "earlier this week", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "35:e1", "article": 35, "input_id": "gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c", "title": "Palantir’s NVIDIA AI Collab Could Be a Game-Changer That Marks a Turn in the Stock", "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-03", "summary": "Palantir has inked a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build AI models for the U.S. government, described as the latest (and expanded) partnership between the two companies targeting sovereign AI. No deal value, contract term, or revenue figure is disclosed.", "passages": ["With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government, it feels like the shorts, like Dr. Burry, have one extra thing to be worried about, as they feel just a bit of a squeeze.", "Either way, the company's latest partnership with Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) brings together two of the biggest winners from the AI boom."], "verified_passages": ["With Palantir now inking a deal to use Nvidia's Nemotron to build models for the government, it feels like the shorts, like Dr. Burry, have one extra thing to be worried about, as they feel just a bit of a squeeze.", "Either way, the company's latest partnership with Nvidia ( NASDAQ:NVDA ) brings together two of the biggest winners from the AI boom."], "original_party": "Palantir Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "finance.yahoo.com", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "61:e1", "article": 61, "input_id": "gnews:0e3cbf453958ce83fabf7a65", "title": "Nvidia and Palantir Are Bringing Sovereign AI to the U.S. Government. Here's How.", "publisher": "fool.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Nvidia and Palantir Technologies announced a collaboration to bring open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments for U.S. government agencies. The partnership features Palantir's new intelligence engine, built on Palantir's Sovereign AI Operating System (which integrates its Artificial Intelligence Platform) and its Foundry and Apollo platforms, deploying Nvidia's Nemotron open models within secure sovereign systems inside customers' own environments. Nvidia supplies the raw AI capability and hardware foundation, with its models running on its accelerated computing platforms and supported by its AI Enterprise software suite. The item discloses no contract value, named government customer, deployment scale or committed spending.", "passages": ["In a move that underscores the growing convergence of advanced computing hardware and enterprise software platforms, Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.", "The partnership features Palantir's new intelligence engine, which deploys Nvidia's Nemotron open models within secure, sovereign systems inside customers' own environments. The engine is built on Palantir's Sovereign AI Operating System, which integrates the company's Artificial Intelligence Platform (AIP).", "The result is an end-to-end solution: Nvidia supplies the raw AI capability and hardware foundation, while Palantir provides the governance, integration, and operational frameworks required in sensitive environments."], "verified_passages": ["In a move that underscores the growing convergence of advanced computing hardware and enterprise software platforms, Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.", "The partnership features Palantir's new intelligence engine, which deploys Nvidia's Nemotron open models within secure, sovereign systems inside customers' own environments. The engine is built on Palantir's Sovereign AI Operating System, which integrates the company's Artificial Intelligence Platform (AIP).", "The result is an end-to-end solution: Nvidia supplies the raw AI capability and hardware foundation, while Palantir provides the governance, integration, and operational frameworks required in sensitive environments."], "original_party": "Nvidia and Palantir Technologies", "reporting_speaker": "Adam Spatacco (fool.com)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "80:e1", "article": 80, "input_id": "gnews:1a116fecd5de1747cc5a06b1", "title": "Palantir (PLTR) Partners with Nvidia For Secure AI Offerings", "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-07", "summary": "Palantir Technologies announced in early July 2026 ('earlier this week') that it is combining its new intelligence engine with Nvidia Corp.'s Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI to U.S. government agencies and major infrastructure operators, with the platform letting agencies tailor the Nemotron models on their own data and retain ownership of model weights; CEO Alex Karp had highlighted the Nvidia partnership in a July 1, 2026 interview as addressing customers' IP and trust concerns.", "passages": ["On July 1, Alex Karp, the Chief Executive Officer of Palantir Technologies Inc. (NASDAQ:PLTR) highlighted the company's recent partnership with Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) to provide safe AI services to U.S. government agencies, allies, and enterprises across the globe.", "Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.", "This new platform allows agencies to tailor Nemotron models using their own data, maintain model weight ownership, and enhance performance via feedback."], "verified_passages": ["On July 1, Alex Karp, the Chief Executive Officer of Palantir Technologies Inc. (NASDAQ:PLTR) highlighted the company's recent partnership with Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) to provide safe AI services to U.S. government agencies, allies, and enterprises across the globe.", "Earlier this week, Palantir announced that it is combining its new intelligence engine and Nvidia's Nemotron open AI models to deliver mission-focused AI for government agencies and major infrastructure operators in the U.S.", "This new platform allows agencies to tailor Nemotron models using their own data, maintain model weight ownership, and enhance performance via feedback."], "original_party": "Palantir Technologies Inc.", "reporting_speaker": "finance.yahoo.com (reporting Palantir's announcement and Alex Karp's CNBC interview)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "earlier this week (announcement); July 1 (Karp interview)", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v2": "61:e1"}, "revises": []}, "12:e1": {"original": {"id": "12:e1", "article": 12, "input_id": "gnews:cdd5ccd6fd57b79e703bfb7d", "title": "Nvidia offers revenue sharing model for aspiring AI start-ups", "publisher": "sg.finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Nvidia CFO Colette Kress, in a blog post, said Nvidia plans a revenue-sharing model that grants token credits to developers in exchange for a share of their future sales, and will connect AI data-centre operators with cloud service providers, establishing a new recurring \"usage-linked earnings stream\" for Nvidia. Under its \"DSX AI factories\" branding, a start-up can access a cloud provider's compute (naming Firmus Technologies) with greater speed and flexibility than building its own capacity. No financial amounts or firm commitments were disclosed.", "passages": ["Nvidia Corp is looking to expand access to its leading AI hardware by granting token credits to developers in exchange for a share of their future sales.", "The company at the heart of the AI boom will help connect AI data centre operators with cloud service providers, simplifying the process for each side and establishing a new recurring \"usagelinked earnings stream\" for itself, chief financial officer Colette Kress wrote in a blog post on Wednesday. The aim of its new revenue-sharing model is to build business among researchers and nascent companies without the capital to access large-scale AI resources.", "Under the company's branding of DSX AI factories, an aspiring AI start-up can access the cloud compute resources of a provider like Firmus Technologies with greater speed and flexibility than would otherwise be the case, Kress said."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia Corp is looking to expand access to its leading AI hardware by granting token credits to developers in exchange for a share of their future sales.", "The company at the heart of the AI boom will help connect AI data centre operators with cloud service providers, simplifying the process for each side and establishing a new recurring \"usagelinked earnings stream\" for itself, chief financial officer Colette Kress wrote in a blog post on Wednesday. The aim of its new revenue-sharing model is to build business among researchers and nascent companies without the capital to access large-scale AI resources.", "Under the company's branding of DSX AI factories, an aspiring AI start-up can access the cloud compute resources of a provider like Firmus Technologies with greater speed and flexibility than would otherwise be the case, Kress said."], "original_party": "Nvidia Corp", "reporting_speaker": "Colette Kress (Nvidia CFO), via blog post", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "Wednesday", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "17:e1", "article": 17, "input_id": "gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563", "title": "Nvidia taps AI cloud providers to expand compute access for startups", "publisher": "cnbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia announced a partnership program that uses its network of AI cloud service providers to give fast-growing AI startups access to compute infrastructure; under the program, cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which positions itself as an intermediary giving startups access to full-stack computing on Nvidia chips.", "passages": ["Chipmaker Nvidia is expanding its support for fast-growing AI startups by introducing a partnership program that leverages its network of AI cloud service providers to offer these firms access to critical computing infrastructure, the company said Thursday.", "Cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which is positioning itself as an intermediary helping startups gain direct access to full-stack computing powered by Nvidia chips."], "verified_passages": ["Chipmaker Nvidia is expanding its support for fast-growing AI startups by introducing a partnership program that leverages its network of AI cloud service providers to offer these firms access to critical computing infrastructure, the company said Thursday.", "Cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which is positioning itself as an intermediary helping startups gain direct access to full-stack computing powered by Nvidia chips."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "CNBC", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-02", "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v1"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "54:e4", "article": 54, "input_id": "gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e", "title": "Jim Cramer Says Buy Nvidia as Chipmaker Rejects 2028 AI Delay Claims", "publisher": "finance.yahoo.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Nvidia had recently launched a revenue-sharing compute program aimed at AI startups, according to the article; no size, terms, counterparties or launch date are given.", "passages": ["The chipmaker, fresh off launching a revenue-sharing compute program for AI startups, has faced this script before."], "verified_passages": ["The chipmaker, fresh off launching a revenue-sharing compute program for AI startups, has faced this script before."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "finance.yahoo.com (Lockridge Okoth, beincrypto.com)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v9"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v1": "17:e1", "v9": "54:e4"}, "revises": []}, "13:e1": {"original": {"id": "13:e1", "article": 13, "input_id": "gnews:26325b9e051efe16db34f758", "title": "Verkada Accelerates Physical AI with NVIDIA", "publisher": "prnewswire.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-01", "summary": "Verkada announced that NVIDIA joins as a new investor in Verkada, following a strategic investment by Alphabet's CapitalG at the end of last year; no investment amount was disclosed.", "passages": ["Verkada is scaling its physical AI platform across more than 2.4 million devices globally with a new technical collaboration and investment from NVIDIA", "NVIDIA also joins as a new investor in Verkada, following a strategic investment from Alphabet's CapitalG at the end of last year."], "verified_passages": ["Verkada is scaling its physical AI platform across more than 2.4 million devices globally with a new technical collaboration and investment from NVIDIA", "NVIDIA also joins as a new investor in Verkada, following a strategic investment from Alphabet's CapitalG at the end of last year."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "Verkada / PR Newswire press release", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1, 2026", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "17:e4": {"original": {"id": "17:e4", "article": 17, "input_id": "gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563", "title": "Nvidia taps AI cloud providers to expand compute access for startups", "publisher": "cnbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia said earlier (in the month before the July 2, 2026 article) that it was aiming to raise debt, which sources said could amount to at least $20 billion, with proceeds intended for general corporate purposes including repayment and refinancing of existing debt.", "passages": ["Nvidia earlier this month said it was aiming to raise debt, which sources said could amount to at least $20 billion. The firm intends to use the proceeds from the offering for general corporate purposes, including repayment and refinancing of existing debt."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia earlier this month said it was aiming to raise debt, which sources said could amount to at least $20 billion. The firm intends to use the proceeds from the offering for general corporate purposes, including repayment and refinancing of existing debt."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "CNBC (citing unnamed sources for the amount)", "tier": "rumour", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "earlier this month", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [{"measure": "debt offering proceeds", "period": null, "value": "at least $20 billion", "kind": "estimate", "basis": "Sources said; proceeds intended for general corporate purposes, including repayment and refinancing of existing debt"}], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {}, "revises": []}, "19:e1": {"original": {"id": "19:e1", "article": 19, "input_id": "gnews:a6ed98dfdf1ad76f6edffdfd", "title": "Singapore seizes $42m mansion over Nvidia chip smuggling", "publisher": "bbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Singapore police seized a luxury home that last sold for S$55 million (£32m; $42.5m) and was allegedly bought with at least two-thirds of its purchase price funded by proceeds from smuggling Nvidia AI chips, as part of a probe into alleged illegal trade in servers containing advanced Nvidia chips that are subject to US export controls; police said an order barred the property's sale during the investigation.", "passages": ["Police in Singapore have seized a multi-million dollar luxury home that was allegedly bought using proceeds from smuggling Nvidia artificial intelligence (AI) chips.", "The property last changed hands for 55 million Singapore dollars (£32m; $42.5m), with at least two-thirds of its purchase price allegedly funded by illicit earnings, authorities said on Wednesday.", "The home was seized as part of a probe into the alleged illegal trade in servers containing highly sought-after advanced Nvidia chips, which are subject to US export controls.", "The police said an order was in place to stop the property being sold during the investigation."], "verified_passages": ["Police in Singapore have seized a multi-million dollar luxury home that was allegedly bought using proceeds from smuggling Nvidia artificial intelligence (AI) chips.", "The property last changed hands for 55 million Singapore dollars (£32m; $42.5m), with at least two-thirds of its purchase price allegedly funded by illicit earnings, authorities said on Wednesday.", "The home was seized as part of a probe into the alleged illegal trade in servers containing highly sought-after advanced Nvidia chips, which are subject to US export controls.", "The police said an order was in place to stop the property being sold during the investigation."], "original_party": "Singapore police", "reporting_speaker": "BBC", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "Wednesday", "evidence_period": "2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": [], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "29:e1", "article": 29, "input_id": "gnews:1eeceeb212a2c82c2e75e806", "title": "Singaporean Police Seize $42M Bungalow in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe - The Diplomat – Asia-Pacific Current Affairs Magazine", "publisher": "thediplomat.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Singaporean authorities said yesterday (reported by The Diplomat on 2026-07-02) that they seized a luxury bungalow valued at about S$55 million (US$42.4 million) under a 'prohibition of disposal order' and seized around S$1 million of funds, and charged four people with money laundering and fraud as part of an investigation linked to the alleged movement of Nvidia chips subject to U.S. export controls.", "passages": ["Singaporean authorities said yesterday that they have seized a luxury bungalow and charged four people with money laundering as part of an investigation linked to the alleged movement of Nvidia chips subject to U.S. export controls.", "In a statement , the Singapore Police Force (SPF) said that it had issued a “prohibition of disposal order” against a residence valued at around S$55 million ($42.4 million) and seized around S$1 million of funds in connection with fraud investigations. The order means the property cannot be sold or transferred as long as it is in force."], "verified_passages": ["Singaporean authorities said yesterday that they have seized a luxury bungalow and charged four people with money laundering as part of an investigation linked to the alleged movement of Nvidia chips subject to U.S. export controls.", "In a statement , the Singapore Police Force (SPF) said that it had issued a “prohibition of disposal order” against a residence valued at around S$55 million ($42.4 million) and seized around S$1 million of funds in connection with fraud investigations. The order means the property cannot be sold or transferred as long as it is in force."], "original_party": "Singapore Police Force", "reporting_speaker": "The Diplomat (Sebastian Strangio)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "yesterday", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "30:e1", "article": 30, "input_id": "gnews:3345f0d91321165a099860c9", "title": "Singapore Seizes $42M Mansion in Nvidia Chip Smuggling Probe｜Daily News Digest｜2026-07-02｜web only", "publisher": "english.cw.com.tw", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Singapore authorities issued a prohibition of disposal order against a luxury home valued at about SGD 55 million ($42 million), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale, and seized about SGD 1 million in bank accounts under investigation, as part of a case of suspected cross-border smuggling of hardware containing Nvidia chips. Lim Jenny and Woon Guo Jie Aaron, two people suspected of involvement in the alleged smuggling, face money laundering charges, and three individuals were brought to court on July 1 and charged with various offences including fraud and money laundering.", "passages": ["Singapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected cross-border smuggling of hardware containing Nvidia chips.", "A prohibition of disposal order was issued against the luxury home, valued at about SGD 55M ($42M), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale. Funds in bank accounts under investigation, valued at about SGD 1M, were also seized.", "Lim Jenny and Woon Guo Jie Aaron, two people suspected of involvement in the alleged smuggling, face money laundering charges.", "Three individuals were also hauled to court on July 1 and charged with various offences, including fraud and money laundering."], "verified_passages": ["Singapore authorities have seized a multimillion-dollar mansion and charged people with money laundering as part of a case of suspected cross-border smuggling of hardware containing Nvidia chips.", "A prohibition of disposal order was issued against the luxury home, valued at about SGD 55M ($42M), freezing the asset and preventing its purchase or sale. Funds in bank accounts under investigation, valued at about SGD 1M, were also seized.", "Lim Jenny and Woon Guo Jie Aaron, two people suspected of involvement in the alleged smuggling, face money laundering charges.", "Three individuals were also hauled to court on July 1 and charged with various offences, including fraud and money laundering."], "original_party": "Singapore authorities", "reporting_speaker": "CommonWealth Magazine", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "94:e1", "article": 94, "input_id": "gnews:c6445931955f107b551cce85", "title": "$42M Singapore mansion seized in Nvidia AI chip smuggling case", "publisher": "e.vnexpress.net", "publication_date": "2026-07-07", "summary": "The Singapore Police Force issued a prohibition of disposal order on July 1 (2026) freezing any sale or transfer of a S$55 million (US$42.5 million) Good Class Bungalow at 12 Chee Hoon Avenue, Singapore, allegedly bought with the proceeds of a scheme to smuggle servers believed to contain Nvidia AI chips that Washington bars from export to China; officers also seized about S$1 million from bank accounts tied to the case, per Channel News Asia.", "passages": ["Singapore police have seized a S$55 million (US$42.5 million) luxury bungalow allegedly bought with the proceeds of a scheme to smuggle servers believed to contain Nvidia artificial intelligence chips that Washington bars from export to China.", "The Singapore Police Force issued a prohibition of disposal order on July 1 freezing any sale or transfer of the Good Class Bungalow, the city-state's most exclusive class of home, at 12 Chee Hoon Avenue near the Singapore Botanic Gardens.", "Officers also seized about S$1 million from bank accounts tied to the case, Channel News Asia reported."], "verified_passages": ["Singapore police have seized a S$55 million (US$42.5 million) luxury bungalow allegedly bought with the proceeds of a scheme to smuggle servers believed to contain Nvidia artificial intelligence chips that Washington bars from export to China.", "The Singapore Police Force issued a prohibition of disposal order on July 1 freezing any sale or transfer of the Good Class Bungalow, the city-state's most exclusive class of home, at 12 Chee Hoon Avenue near the Singapore Botanic Gardens.", "Officers also seized about S$1 million from bank accounts tied to the case, Channel News Asia reported."], "original_party": "Singapore Police Force", "reporting_speaker": "e.vnexpress.net (citing Channel News Asia)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": "Order issued 