ed Nvidia from selling China the chip, which it launched in 2023, due to export controls the Biden administration put in place."], "original_party": "Trump administration", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "last December", "evidence_period": "December 2025", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17", "v8"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, {"id": "212:e2", "article": 212, "input_id": "gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a", "title": "U.S. trade official says 'very few' Nvidia H200 AI chips have been shipped to China", "publisher": "cnbc.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-14", "summary": "President Donald Trump said in December that the U.S. government would approve China sales of Nvidia's H200 AI chip in exchange for a 25% cut, and licences for the chips were issued earlier this year (before the July 14, 2026 article).", "passages": ["In December, President Donald Trump said that the U.S. government would approve China sales of the H200 AI chip in exchange for a 25% cut. Licenses for the chips, which some in the administration say can be used for military purposes, were issued earlier this year ."], "verified_passages": ["In December, President Donald Trump said that the U.S. government would approve China sales of the H200 AI chip in exchange for a 25% cut. Licenses for the chips, which some in the administration say can be used for military purposes, were issued earlier this year ."], "original_party": "President Donald Trump / U.S. government", "reporting_speaker": "CNBC", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": "December", "evidence_period": "policy in force in 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17", "v8"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v17": "19:e2", "v8": "19:e2"}, "revises": []}, "21:e4": {"original": {"id": "21:e4", "article": 21, "input_id": "gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816", "title": "Nvidia offers to take a cut of AI cloud revenue on top of hardware sales in new opt