g commercial performance obligations."], "verified_passages": ["Plus, Microsoft's Azure remains a formidable growth engine, with a staggering $627 billion in remaining commercial performance obligations."], "original_party": "Microsoft", "reporting_speaker": "Justin Pope (Motley Fool)", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v4"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v4": "22:e4"}, "revises": []}, "24:e1": {"original": {"id": "24:e1", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia presented a report to the U.S. government arguing that Huawei's stockpile of AI chips, together with growing capacity at its manufacturing partner SMIC, give Huawei \"the flexibility to satisfy global AI chip demand,\" and warning that \"if Nvidia is kept out of the China market, Huawei production and sales will soar.\" The report gave no timeframe and did not address performance differences between Nvidia and Huawei chips.", "passages": ["In a report that Nvidia presented to the U.S. government — which The Wire has reviewed — the company warned that Huawei’s stockpile of chips, along with growing capacity at its manufacturing partner Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. (SMIC), give it “the flexibility to satisfy global AI chip demand.”", "“If Nvidia is kept out of the China market, Huawei production and sales will soar,” the report said, although it did not specify a timeframe or refer to the differences in performance between Nvidia and Huawei chips."], "verified_passages": ["In a report that Nvidia presented to the U.S. government — which The Wire has reviewed — the company warned that Huawei’s stockpile of chips, along with growing capacity at its manufacturing partner Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. (SMIC), give it “the flexibility to satisfy global AI chip demand.”", "“If Nvidia is kept out of the China market, Huawei production and sales will soar,” the report said, although it did not specify a timeframe or refer to the differences in performance between Nvidia and Huawei chips."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China (Noah Berman)", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v6"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v6": "24:e1"}, "revises": []}, "24:e3": {"original": {"id": "24:e3", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has said that, since the Biden administration first imposed AI-chip export controls in 2022, Nvidia's market share in China has fallen to zero.", "passages": ["Since the Biden administration first imposed export controls on AI chips in 2022, Nvidia’s market share in China has fallen to zero, Huang has said ."], "verified_passages": ["Since the Biden administration first imposed export controls on AI chips in 2022, Nvidia’s market share in China has fallen to zero, Huang has said ."], "original_party": "Jensen Huang (NVIDIA)", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "since 2022 export controls", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v17": "24:e3"}, "revises": []}, "24:e4": {"original": {"id": "24:e4", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "In the report presented to the U.S. government, Nvidia estimated that Huawei sold between 200,000 and 450,000 AI chips in 2024 and would sell 1 million in 2025.", "passages": ["In the report it presented to the government, Nvidia estimated that Huawei sold between 200,000 and 450,000 AI chips in 2024 and that it would sell 1 million in 2025."], "verified_passages": ["In the report it presented to the government, Nvidia estimated that Huawei sold between 200,000 and 450,000 AI chips in 2024 and that it would sell 1 million in 2025."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "2024 and 2025", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v6"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v6": "24:e4"}, "revises": []}, "24:e5": {"original": {"id": "24:e5", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Nvidia's report estimated that by the end of 2026 SMIC will have made more than 700,000 of Huawei's Ascend 910C chips, reaching production of 50,000 of these chips per month, and that by 2027 SMIC would produce several million of Huawei's less advanced 910B chips.", "passages": ["It also estimated that by the end of this year SMIC — which manufactures chips based on Huawei’s design and technology — will have made more than 700,000 Ascend 910C chips, one of Huawei’s most advanced, with production reaching 50,000 of these chips per month. By 2027, the report said, SMIC would be producing several million of Huawei’s less advanced 910B chips."], "verified_passages": ["It also estimated that by the end of this year SMIC — which manufactures chips based on Huawei’s design and technology — will have made more than 700,000 Ascend 910C chips, one of Huawei’s most advanced, with production reaching 50,000 of these chips per month. By 2027, the report said, SMIC would be producing several million of Huawei’s less advanced 910B chips."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "end-2026 and 2027", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v6"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v6": "24:e5"}, "revises": []}, "24:e6": {"original": {"id": "24:e6", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "Chris McGuire of the Council on Foreign Relations estimated that if Huawei made 800,000 Ascend 910C chips in 2025, that would amount to just 5.3 percent of the total processing power of Nvidia's chip production that year, and that Nvidia's performance lead will only grow even if Huawei makes 2 million AI chips in 2026 and 4 million in 2027.", "passages": ["In a report published in December, Chris McGuire , a senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations, estimated that if Huawei made 800,000 Ascend 910C chips in 2025 — a figure at the high end of several estimates — that would amount to just 5.3 percent of the total processing power of Nvidia’s chip production that year.", "McGuire also estimates that Nvidia’s lead by performance will only grow, even if Huawei were to make 2 million AI chips this year and 4 million in 2027."], "verified_passages": ["In a report published in December, Chris McGuire , a senior fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations, estimated that if Huawei made 800,000 Ascend 910C chips in 2025 — a figure at the high end of several estimates — that would amount to just 5.3 percent of the total processing power of Nvidia’s chip production that year.", "McGuire also estimates that Nvidia’s lead by performance will only grow, even if Huawei were to make 2 million AI chips this year and 4 million in 2027."], "original_party": "Chris McGuire (Council on Foreign Relations)", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "2025, 2026 and 2027", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v6"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v6": "24:e6"}, "revises": []}, "24:e7": {"original": {"id": "24:e7", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summary": "According to research institute Epoch AI, Huawei made just 6 percent of the total AI chips sold worldwide in the first quarter of 2026, and about half that amount after adjusting for the fact that its chips are less powerful than Nvidia's.", "passages": ["Huawei made just 6 percent of the total AI chips sold worldwide during the first quarter of this year, and half that amount after adjusting for the fact that the company’s chips are not as powerful as Nvidia’s, according to Epoch AI, a research institute."], "verified_passages": ["Huawei made just 6 percent of the total AI chips sold worldwide during the first quarter of this year, and half that amount after adjusting for the fact that the company’s chips are not as powerful as Nvidia’s, according to Epoch AI, a research institute."], "original_party": "Epoch AI", "reporting_speaker": "The Wire China", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Q1 calendar 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v6"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v6": "24:e7"}, "revises": []}, "24:e8": {"original": {"id": "24:e8", "article": 24, "input_id": "gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02", "title": "Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case", "publisher": "thewirechina.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-02", "summa