article reports that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply and that device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products, attributing the pressure to constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand.", "passages": ["Contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply, and device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products."], "verified_passages": ["Contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply, and device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products."], "original_party": "MarketScale", "reporting_speaker": "MarketScale", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v3", "v5"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v3": "56:e5", "v5": "56:e5"}, "revises": []}, "56:e6": {"original": {"id": "56:e6", "article": 56, "input_id": "gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd", "title": "Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why", "publisher": "marketscale.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, showing procurement structure materially moves final pricing.", "passages": ["Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number."], "verified_passages": ["Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number."], "original_party": "Morgan Stanley Research", "reporting_speaker": "MarketScale", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Vera Rubin (VR200) generation", "figures": [{"measure": "VR200 rack cost with self-sourced memory modules", "period": null, "value": "$6.7 million", "kind": "estimate", "basis": "if hyperscaler self-sources certain memory modules, Morgan Stanley estimate"}], "thesis_ids": ["v1", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v1": "56:e6", "v20": "56:e6"}, "revises": []}, "57:e1": {"original": {"id": "57:e1", "article": 57, "input_id": "gnews:4a892d75e355bee00aa3c572", "title": "Nvidia vs. Palantir: Which Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Is the Better Buy Right Now?", "publisher": "fool.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Nvidia reported, for the first quarter of calendar 2026, record total revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year, with its core data center segment growing 92% year over year to $75.2 billion. In the same earnings report, earnings per share increased 214% year over year and free cash flow rose 86%, as reported by Adam Spatacco of fool.com.", "passages": ["During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year. The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion. Nvidia's accelerating top line wasn't the only highlight from its earnings report. The company's earnings per share (EPS) increased 214% year over year, while free cash flow rose 86%."], "verified_passages": ["During the first quarter of calendar 2026, Nvidia generated record revenue of $81.6 billion -- up 85% year over year. The company's core data center segment grew even faster, at 92% year over year, to $75.2 billion. Nvidia's accelerating top line wasn't the only highlight from its earnings report. The company's earnings per share (EPS) increased 214% year over year, while free cash flow rose 86%."], "original_party": "Nvidia", "reporting_speaker": "Adam Spatacco, fool.com", "tier": "fact", "state