ooling, networking, and the other plumbing required to run AI at scale."], "verified_passages": ["Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031. That spending includes chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking, and the other plumbing required to run AI at scale."], "original_party": "Goldman Sachs", "reporting_speaker": "Allen Harris, The Berkshire Edge", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "calendar 2026 and 2031; cumulative 2026-2031", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["clean-2", "v1", "v2", "v22"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"clean-2": "66:e4", "v1": "66:e4", "v2": "66:e4", "v22": "66:e4"}, "revises": []}, "67:e1": {"original": {"id": "67:e1", "article": 67, "input_id": "gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb", "title": "A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water", "publisher": "autonocion.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "On July 1, 2026, Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell-based Nvidia Spark desktop unit to its Ward 250 TRISO high-temperature gas microreactor at the San Rafael Energy Lab outside Orangeville, Utah, and served a website off the electricity. Valar says the reactor ran at 37% of its intended output, which CEO Isaiah Taylor put at roughly 100 kilowatts of thermal energy. Bloomberg noted the electricity was tiny but confirmed it was the first time a next-generation reactor produced power to run an AI chip in the US.", "passages": ["the event a nuclear startup and Nvidia staged in the Utah desert on July 1 was aimed squarely at that mood. Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell -based Nvidia desktop unit to its Ward 250 microreactor, served a website off the electricity, and announced a plan for something much bigger that skips the local water entirely.", "On stage at the San Rafael Energy Lab outside Orangeville, a Valar team member plugged an Nvidia Spark desktop unit, running the company’s Blackwell architecture, into a circuit fed from the reactor hall.", "Valar says the reactor was running at 37% of its intended output during the show, which founder and CEO Isaiah Taylor put at roughly 100 kilowatts of thermal energy.", "Bloomberg noted the output amounted to a tiny amount of electricity, and confirmed the part that matters: it’s the first time a next-generation reactor has produced power to run an AI chip in the US."], "verified_passages": ["the event a nuclear startup and Nvidia staged in the Utah desert on July 1 was aimed squarely at that mood. Valar Atomics wired a Blackwell -based Nvidia desktop unit to its Ward 250 microreactor, served a website off the electricity, and announced a plan for something much bigger that skips the local water entirely.", "On stage at the San Rafael Energy Lab outside Orangeville, a Valar team member plugged an Nvidia Spark desktop unit, running the company’s Blackwell architecture, into a circuit fed from the reactor hall.", "Valar says the reactor was running at 37% of its intended output during the show, which founder and CEO Isaiah Taylor put at roughly 100 kilowatts of thermal energy.", "Bloomberg noted the output amounted to a tiny amount of electricity, and confirmed the part that matters: it’s the first time a next-generation reactor has produced power to run an AI chip in the US."], "original_party": "Valar Atomics (reactor), with Nvidia hardware", "reporting_speaker": "autonocion.com (Luis Reyes), citing Bloomberg and Tom's Hardware", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-01", "statement_date_text": "July 1", "evidence_period": "2026-07-01 (one-day demonstration)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["clean-2"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"clean-2": "67:e1"}, "revises": []}, "67:e3": {"original": {"id": "67:e3", "article": 67, "input_id": "gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb", "title": "A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water", "publisher": "autonocion.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "According to a running tally at Tom's Hardware, more than 75 US data-center projects worth around $130 billion have been blocked or delayed so far this year, and polling in the same reporting found 7 in 10 Americans say they do not want a data center built near their home.", "passages": ["With over $130 billion in data center projects already blocked or delayed by communities fed up with power and water demands, a zero-local-water nuclear option isn't just an engineering story — it's a potential unlock for the entire AI buildout.", "More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware . Polling covered in the same reporting has 7 out of 10 Americans saying they don’t want one built anywhere near their home."], "verified_passages": ["With over $130 billion in data center projects already blocked or delayed by communities fed up with power and water demands, a zero-local-water nuclear option isn't just an engineering story — it's a potential unlock for the entire AI buildout.", "More than 75 of these projects, worth around $130 billion, have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom’s Hardware . Polling covered in the same reporting has 7 out of 10 Americans saying they don’t want one built anywhere near their home."], "original_party": "Tom's Hardware (running tally and polling)", "reporting_speaker": "auto