y incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets."], "verified_passages": ["Bleeding Edge plans to expand both the capacity of its neocloud and its AI Factories in the coming months by incorporating new Nvidia systems and deploying infrastructure in other strategic markets."], "original_party": "Bleeding Edge", "reporting_speaker": "datacenterdynamics.com (Cristina Cueto, DCD)", "tier": "party_statement", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "coming months (no specific date given)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v2", "v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v2": "68:e3", "v20": "68:e3"}, "revises": []}, "69:e4": {"original": {"id": "69:e4", "article": 69, "input_id": "gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96", "title": "Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop", "publisher": "the-decoder.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology, which links many chips into a single large system, will not arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman, meaning Nvidia has no proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now.", "passages": ["A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman. That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now."], "verified_passages": ["A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman. That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now."], "original_party": "SemiAnalysis", "reporting_speaker": "the-decoder.com, citing SemiAnalysis", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Feynman generation (the generation after next)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v18"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [{"id": "75:e7", "article": 75, "input_id": "gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571", "title": "Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "SemiAnalysis placed a fully production-ready co-packaged optics NVSwitch no earlier than the Feynman generation that follows Rubin, leaving copper as the only near-term solution for linking Rubin Ultra at rack scale.", "passages": ["SemiAnalysis has also placed a fully production-ready co-packaged optics NVSwitch no earlier than the Feynman generation that follows Rubin, which leaves copper as the only near-term solution for linking Rubin Ultra at rack scale and thereby puts even more weight on the PCB midplane."], "verified_passages": ["SemiAnalysis has also placed a fully production-ready co-packaged optics NVSwitch no earlier than the Feynman generation that follows Rubin, which leaves copper as the only near-term solution for linking Rubin Ultra at rack scale and thereby puts even more weight on the PCB midplane."], "original_party": "SemiAnalysis", "reporting_speaker": "Luke James, Tom's Hardware", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": null, "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v18"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}], "links": {"v18": "69:e4"}, "revises": []}, "69:e5": {"original": {"id": "69:e5", "article": 69, "input_id": "gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96", "title": "Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop", "publisher": "the-decoder.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "According to SemiAnalysis, Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall from the scrapped and delayed next-generation rack configurations by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.", "passages": ["Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor."], "verified_passages": ["Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor."], "original_party": "NVIDIA", "reporting_speaker": "the-decoder.com, citing SemiAnalysis", "tier": "third_party_view", "statement_date": null, "statement_date_text": null, "evidence_period": "Not stated (plan covering Rubin-generation Oberon racks)", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v20"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v20": "69:e5"}, "revises": []}, "74:e1": {"original": {"id": "74:e1", "article": 74, "input_id": "gnews:f0d529209a91c7a237e117f1", "title": "Nvidia chips case: Man charged with fraud allegedly used over $38m in ill-gotten gains to buy house", "publisher": "straitstimes.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "On 6 July 2026, Singapore authorities handed Alan Wei Zhaolun, 50, the Singaporean former chief executive of A-Speed Infotech, Aperia International and Aperia Cloud Services (II), nine additional charges – three counts of money laundering and six counts of fraud – bringing his total to 11 charges; on the same day the three linked companies were also charged with fraud (Aperia International five counts, Aperia Cloud Services (II) two, A-Speed Infotech one). Wei is accused of using more than $38 million of alleged ill-gotten gains to buy a landed property in Chee Hoon Avenue between July and October 2024, a good-class bungalow police earlier valued at around $55 million, and of acquiring more than $5 million in two bank accounts that year, about $3.2 million of which is alleged to be the benefits of purported criminal conduct. The item describes the case as allegedly linked to chipmaker Nvidia. Wei's lawyers said he and the companies will contest all charges; pre-trial conferences are set for 14 August.", "passages": ["SINGAPORE – A man accused of fraud in a case allegedly linked to chipmaker Nvidia is said to have used more than $38 million in purported ill-gotten gains to buy a landed property.", "On July 6, Alan Wei Zhaolun, 50, was handed nine additional charges – three counts of money laundering and six counts of fraud.", "The Singaporean former chief executive of a group of companies – A-Speed Infotech, Aperia International and Aperia Cloud Services (II) – now faces 11 charges in all.", "He is accused of using more than $38 million of alleged ill-gotten gains to buy the house in Chee Hoon Avenue, near Adam Road, between July and October 2024.", "In an earlier statement, the police said that the good-class bungalow was valued at around $55 million.", "Wei is also said to have acquired more than $5 million in total in two bank accounts that year.", "Around $3.2 million of the amount is alleged to be the benefits of purported criminal conduct.", "On July 6, Aperia International was charged with five counts of fraud, while Aperia Cloud Services (II) was handed two such charges. A-Speed Infotech was charged with one count of fraud.", "The pre-trial conferences for the three companies and Wei will be held on Aug 14.", "In a statement on July 6, they said their client and the companies will be contesting all the charges against them."], "verified_passages": ["SINGAPORE – A man accused of fraud in a case allegedly linked to chipmaker Nvidia is said to have used more than $38 million in purported ill-gotten gains to buy a landed property.", "On July 6, Alan Wei Zhaolun, 50, was handed nine additional charges – three counts of money laundering and six counts of fraud.", "The Singaporean former chief executive of a group of companies – A-Speed Infotech, Aperia International and Aperia Cloud Services (II) – now faces 11 charges in all.", "He is accused of using more than $38 million of alleged ill-gotten gains to buy the house in Chee Hoon Avenue, near Adam Road, between July and October 2024.", "In an earlier statement, the police said that the good-class bungalow was valued at around $55 million.", "Wei is also said to have acquired more than $5 million in total in two bank accounts that year.", "Around $3.2 million of the amount is alleged to be the benefits of purported criminal conduct.", "On July 6, Aperia International was charged with five counts of fraud, while Aperia Cloud Services (II) was handed two such charges.\nA-Speed Infotech was charged with one count of fraud.", "The pre-trial conferences for the three companies and Wei will be held on Aug 14.", "In a statement on July 6, they said their client and the companies will be contesting all the charges against them."], "original_party": "Singapore Police Force / Singapore courts (charges against Alan Wei Zhaolun and three Aperia-linked companies)", "reporting_speaker": "The Straits Times", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-06", "statement_date_text": "July 6", "evidence_period": "Alleged conduct July–October 2024; charges filed 6 July 2026", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v17": "74:e1"}, "revises": []}, "74:e2": {"original": {"id": "74:e2", "article": 74, "input_id": "gnews:f0d529209a91c7a237e117f1", "title": "Nvidia chips case: Man charged with fraud allegedly used over $38m in ill-gotten gains to buy house", "publisher": "straitstimes.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", "summary": "Singapore police said the fraud charges allege that Alan Wei Zhaolun conspired with Aaron Woon Guo Jie, 41, and Jenny Lim, 51, to commit fraud multiple times in 2023 and 2024, in a conspiracy linked to the purchase of servers from three suppliers – Dell, Super Micro Computer and Asus – in which they falsely represented in communications to those suppliers that one of the Aperia Group companies would be the end-user of the servers. The charges are allegations; the defendants contest them.", "passages": ["According to his latest charges, he also allegedly conspired with Aaron Woon Guo Jie, 41, and Jenny Lim, 51, to commit fraud multiple times in 2023 and 2024.", "The police said the fraud charges allege that the trio engaged in a conspiracy to commit fraud linked to the purchase of servers from three suppliers – Dell, Super Micro Computer and Asus.", "Without revealing further details, a police spokesperson added: “The charges asserted that... they falsely represented, in communications to these suppliers, that one of the Aperia Group companies would be the end-user of the servers.”"], "verified_passages": ["According to his latest charges, he also allegedly conspired with Aaron Woon Guo Jie, 41, and Jenny Lim, 51, to commit fraud multiple times in 2023 and 2024.", "The police said the fraud charges allege that the trio engaged in a conspiracy to commit fraud linked to the purchase of servers from three suppliers – Dell, Super Micro Computer and Asus.", "Without revealing further details, a police spokesperson added: “The charges asserted that... they falsely represented, in communications to these suppliers, that one of the Aperia Group companies would be the end-user of the servers.”"], "original_party": "Singapore Police Force (charge allegations)", "reporting_speaker": "The Straits Times, citing a police spokesperson", "tier": "fact", "statement_date": "2026-07-06", "statement_date_text": "July 6", "evidence_period": "2023 and 2024", "figures": [], "thesis_ids": ["v17"], "unresolved_thesis_ids": []}, "members": [], "links": {"v17": "74:e2"}, "revises": []}, "75:e5": {"original": {"id": "75:e5", "article": 75, "input_id": "gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571", "title": "Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]", "publisher": "tomshardware.com", "publication_date": "2026-07-06", 