I agree with leaving Jev unchanged for now, with one change: **do not call this line closed or describe the wrong relations as “about 1% of links.”**

1. **Mismatches and limits in [RESULT.md](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/RESULT.md:67):**

   - Line 68 says the **range of implied revenue did not change**, then gives different ranges: $330–340 billion with the statement and $335–370 billion without it. The ranges overlap, but the second extends $30 billion higher.
   - Line 80 calls “about 1% of the links” the measured size of **wrong** revision relations. The count includes correct repeats and uncertain relations. In draw 1, the source readers called only **2 of 700 links** consequences of relations between different statements; the other three were two repeats and one uncertain relation. Draws 2 and 3 were not source-labelled. See [inheritance-census.json](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/inheritance-census.json) and [RESULT.md:53](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/RESULT.md:53).
   - The table should identify draw 3’s completed run as `judged-2`: the original `judged` stopped at 62 judgments and has 118 links. The replacement is recorded in [stage2-frozen.md:77](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-frozen.md:77). I could verify the draw 1 and 2 link totals directly, but did not independently reproduce all draw 2 and 3 carried-link and showing counts.
   - The control report supports 239 matched requests and the compared ledger tables, but excludes `judgements.call_id`; “the ledger … equal” at line 19 is broader than the actual comparison. See [PROTOCOL.md:23](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/PROTOCOL.md:23).

   The replay reports support the first changed request, its four removed lines, the 14 identical requests already built at that level, and the unchanged 14-day replay when the link is retained.

2. **The six answers:** “No difference in the conclusion” is correct **under the registered definition**, which means all six chose rung 2 ([PROTOCOL.md:91](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/PROTOCOL.md:91)). I read `response.choices[0].message.content` in all six files in [judge-probe-1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/judge-probe-1/). All cite the roughly $390 billion Data Center forecast as a basis; they also discuss product shipments or other evidence. None explicitly names the roadmap denial in its reasons. But all three controls cite it and mark it as pushing upward, so the written reasons do **not prove** it had no influence. Counterfactual 2’s $350–370 billion estimate is the material difference hidden by the shared rung.

3. **Strongest challenge:** the link count misses the separately printed “later version” statement: six records have a printed relation the readers called different statements, appearing in **55 showings** in draw 1. That statement can reach the judge even when the new evidence already belongs under the question. It was not tested here ([inheritance-census.json](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/inheritance-census.json); [judging.py:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:130)). Also, this case is one revenue question dominated by a numerical dependency; it does not represent every question or later day. A cheap next check is to read the saved reasons and citations for those six printed relations, alongside the source statements. These limits justify keeping the defect **open**, but do not establish enough impact to restart Jev tuning.

4. **PRD:** Yes. [PRD §6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:182) says a revision saves “**The new evidence and its source, linked to the earlier statement as a revision**”; it does not say to copy the earlier record’s question links. The experimental [adapter](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-2026-11-09/adapter.py:222) explicitly copies them, following the existing [writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:255).

I agree with leaving Jev unchanged, but would keep the defect open and replace the claimed size with the labelled counts and their limits.


